COLLDATA("tadabburen","en",[[438,"§Fatir\ndeeds\nSay, \"O Allah, help me to memorize Your Book, practice it, and invite others to it.\"\nCompete with the congregation in your mosque to be in the first row during prayer.\nShare a message in which you remind others that whoever wants the adornments of Paradise, must refrain from wearing the prohibited adornments in worldly life.\nguid\nDo not be self-admiring, nor think highly of your deeds. Aisha (i) used to consider herself among those who wrong themselves.\nBe aware that whomever Allah has chosen will make him to inherit the knowledge and practice of the Book; therefore, try to be among them.\nReflect of the fact that our Lord, the Almighty, has included those who wrong themselves among His chosen people.\nrefl\nثُمَّ أَوۡرَثۡنَا ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ ٱلَّذِينَ ٱصۡطَفَيۡنَا مِنۡ عِبَادِنَاۖ فَمِنۡهُمۡ ظَالِمٞ لِّنَفۡسِهِۦ وَمِنۡهُم مُّقۡتَصِدٞ وَمِنۡهُمۡ سَابِقُۢ بِٱلۡخَيۡرَٰتِ بِإِذۡنِ ٱللَّهِۚ ذَٰلِكَ هُوَ ٱلۡفَضۡلُ ٱلۡكَبِيرُ ٣٢\nOmar, Ibn Masoud, Ibn Abbas, Ka'b, Aisha, and most Quran interpreters said: These three categories are among Muhammad’s (ﷺ) Ummah; the one who wrongs himself is the disobedient, the one who is foremost in good deeds is the pious, and the moderate is in between. Ibn Juzay: 2/217\nTo which Ummah do the above-mentioned three categories belong? What are their qualities?\nوَمِنۡهُم مُّقۡتَصِدٞ وَمِنۡهُمۡ سَابِقُۢ بِٱلۡخَيۡرَٰتِ بِإِذۡنِ ٱللَّهِۚ\nThe phrase (with Allah's permission) refers to those who are foremost in good deeds, lest they become arrogant because of their deeds. It is a reminder that they only became foremost in good deeds with the help of Allah, so they should focus on giving thanks to Allah for the blessings that He has bestowed upon them. Al-Saadi: 689\nThe phrase (with Allah's permission) refers to those who are foremost in good deeds. Why?\nوَقَالُواْ ٱلۡحَمۡدُ لِلَّهِ ٱلَّذِيٓ أَذۡهَبَ عَنَّا ٱلۡحَزَنَۖ إِنَّ رَبَّنَا لَغَفُورٞ شَكُورٌ ٣٤\nIbn Abbas said: It is the sorrow of entering Hellfire. Qatadah said: It is the sorrow of death. Muqatil said: They were sad because they did not know what Allah will do to them. Ikrimah said: It is the sorrow for committing sins, and fear of the rejection of their good deeds. Al-Baghawi: 3/626\nWhat made the believers feel sorrow in worldly life, but Allah will take it away in Paradise?\nٱلَّذِيٓ أَحَلَّنَا دَارَ ٱلۡمُقَامَةِ مِن فَضۡلِهِۦ لَا يَمَسُّنَا فِيهَا نَصَبٞ وَلَا يَمَسُّنَا فِيهَا لُغُوبٞ ٣٥\n(The everlasting home), it is Paradise, the perpetual residence, where they settle therein and never leave. Ibn Juzay: 2/217.\nParadise is called: The everlasting home. Why?\nٱلَّذِيٓ أَحَلَّنَا دَارَ ٱلۡمُقَامَةِ مِن فَضۡلِهِۦ\nMeaning: Allah has given us this position and status out of His grace, blessing, and mercy, for our good deeds were not equivalent to this. Ibn Kathir: 3/535.\nCan a person enter Paradise based solely on his deeds? Explain in light of this verse.\nوَٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ لَهُمۡ نَارُ جَهَنَّمَ لَا يُقۡضَىٰ عَلَيۡهِمۡ فَيَمُوتُواْ وَلَا يُخَفَّفُ عَنۡهُم مِّنۡ عَذَابِهَاۚ كَذَٰلِكَ نَجۡزِي كُلَّ كَفُورٖ ٣٦\n(Death] is not decreed), they will not die, because if they do, all of their senses will stop, and they will be relieved. Ibn Atiyah: 4/440.\nDeath will not be decreed for the dwellers of Hellfire. Why?\nوَهُمۡ يَصۡطَرِخُونَ فِيهَا رَبَّنَآ أَخۡرِجۡنَا نَعۡمَلۡ صَٰلِحًا غَيۡرَ ٱلَّذِي كُنَّا نَعۡمَلُۚ\n(We will do righteous deeds), Ibn Abbas said: It means that we will say \"None is worthy of worship but Allah alone.\" Meaning: We will believe instead of disbelief, obey instead of disobedience, and follow the commands of the Messengers. Al-Qurtubi: 17/388.\nWhat will be the righteous deed that the dwellers of Hellfire wish for?\nwords\nظَالِمٌ لِنَفسِهِHe wrongs himself by committing sins\nمُقتَصِدٌHe performs the duties and avoids what is forbidden\nسَابِقٌ بِالخَيرَاتِHe performs the duties and voluntary righteous deeds\nعَدنٍThe perpetual residence\nلُغُوبٌFatigue, weariness"],[439,"§Fatir\ndeeds\nCollaborate with a friend of yours to do a righteous deed together.\nInvoke Allah by His Names, the Forbearing, the Forgiving, and say, \"O the Forbearing, be Forbearing with me and do not punish me. O the Forgiving, forgive me and have mercy on me.\"\nWatch a documentary film or look at pictures of volcanos, earthquakes, or floods, and reflect on the power of Allah in contrast to the weakness of mankind.\nguid\nDisbelief and disobedience increase the servant in hatred and contempt before Allah.\nBe aware that the wrongdoers' promises to each other are delusion and lies, so, do not be deluded by them.\nRejoice and do not be afraid, as evil plotting encompasses its own people.\nrefl\nهُوَ ٱلَّذِي جَعَلَكُمۡ خَلَٰٓئِفَ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِۚ فَمَن كَفَرَ فَعَلَيۡهِ كُفۡرُهُۥۖ\nIn essence, Allah says: O mankind, whoever among you disbelieves in Allah, will harm only himself, and the punishment for his disbelief will befall no one but him. Al-Tabari: 20/480.\nWho will be harmed by the disbelief of the son of Adam?\nوَلَا يَزِيدُ ٱلۡكَٰفِرِينَ كُفۡرُهُمۡ عِندَ رَبِّهِمۡ إِلَّا مَقۡتٗاۖ\nMeaning: The longer they persist in their disbelief, the more Allah hates them. This is in contrast to the believers, for the longer they live and do good deeds, the higher their status in Paradise will be, the greater their reward, and the more beloved they will be to their Creator. Ibn Kathir: 3/538.\nThe verse mentions the effect of disbelief on the disbelievers; what is the effect of faith on the believers?\nوَأَقۡسَمُواْ بِٱللَّهِ جَهۡدَ أَيۡمَٰنِهِمۡ لَئِن جَآءَهُمۡ نَذِيرٞ لَّيَكُونُنَّ أَهۡدَىٰ مِنۡ إِحۡدَى ٱلۡأُمَمِۖ فَلَمَّا جَآءَهُمۡ نَذِيرٞ مَّا زَادَهُمۡ إِلَّا نُفُورًا ٤٢\nThe oath mentioned was not made for a good purpose or seeking the truth, otherwise they would have been helped to attain that. Rather, it stemmed from arrogance in the land toward other people, and toward the truth, and they used elaborate words when they spoke of that with the aim of deceiving and cheating. They also wanted to give the impression that they were people of truth who were keen to seek it, in order that some people would be deceived by them and others would follow in their footsteps. Al-Saadi: 691.\nWas their mentioned oath made to seek the truth?\nٱسۡتِكۡبَارٗا فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ وَمَكۡرَ ٱلسَّيِّيِٕۚ وَلَا يَحِيقُ ٱلۡمَكۡرُ ٱلسَّيِّئُ إِلَّا بِأَهۡلِهِۦۚ\nDue to their arrogance), insolence toward faith. (And plotting evil), plotting evil deed, which is disbelief, deceiving the oppressed and averting them away from faith in order to increase their followers. Al-Qurtubi: 17/396.\nWhat was their evil plotting that put them under punishment, in order we avoid it?\nٱسۡتِكۡبَارٗا فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ وَمَكۡرَ ٱلسَّيِّيِٕۚ وَلَا يَحِيقُ ٱلۡمَكۡرُ ٱلسَّيِّئُ إِلَّا بِأَهۡلِهِۦۚ فَهَلۡ يَنظُرُونَ إِلَّا سُنَّتَ ٱلۡأَوَّلِينَۚ فَلَن تَجِدَ لِسُنَّتِ ٱللَّهِ تَبۡدِيلٗاۖ وَلَن تَجِدَ لِسُنَّتِ ٱللَّهِ تَحۡوِيلًا ٤٣\nWhen people do not feel safe from each other, they become alienated and turn against each other, causing harm and destruction in order for each one to defeat the other. Eventually, this leads to prevalent corruption in the world, and Allah does not like corruption. Ibn Ashur: 22/335.\nWhat are the effects of losing the sense of security on society? Explain in light of this verse.\nفَهَلۡ يَنظُرُونَ إِلَّا سُنَّتَ ٱلۡأَوَّلِينَۚ فَلَن تَجِدَ لِسُنَّتِ ٱللَّهِ تَبۡدِيلٗاۖ وَلَن تَجِدَ لِسُنَّتِ ٱللَّهِ تَحۡوِيلًا ٤٣\nAllah decreed punishment on the disbelievers and made it His way of dealing with them or others who deserve it. No one can change that, nor can he divert the punishment from himself to another. Al-Qurtubi: 17/400.\nDoes Allah's way change when it comes to punishing those who disobey Him?\nوَمَا كَانَ ٱللَّهُ لِيُعۡجِزَهُۥ مِن شَيۡءٖ فِي ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَلَا فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِۚ إِنَّهُۥ كَانَ عَلِيمٗا قَدِيرٗا ٤٤\nThe inability of one to carry out his will can be either the lack of knowledge, or lack of ability; in both cases, that contravenes Allah's Attributes: The All-Knowing, the Most Capable. Ibn Ashur: 22/339.\nThe verse concludes with Allah's Attributes: The All-Knowing, the Most Capable. Why?\nwords\nخَلاَئِفَSucceeding each other upon the earth\nمَقتًاHatred and contempt\nأَرَأَيتُمTell me\nبَيِّنَةٍ مِنهُClear proof\nغُرُورًاDelusion\nجَهدَ أَيمَانِهِمMost solemn oath\nيَحِيقُEncompasses"],[440,"§Ya-Sin, Fatir\ndeeds\nRecall a sermon that you heard and follow its words of advice, so that you may be given good tidings of forgiveness and a generous reward.\nChoose a deed that will be a legacy after your death and do it today, such as helping to build a mosque, inviting a non-Muslim to Islam, teaching an ignorant person something or akin to that.\nGo to the mosque on foot, and your steps will be recorded for you.\nguid\nBe certain that when someone's death time comes, it will not be delayed for a moment.\nWhoever is rightly doomed, will not benefit from the warning.\nIf you fear the injustice of an oppressor, say:\nrefl\nوَلَوۡ يُؤَاخِذُ ٱللَّهُ ٱلنَّاسَ بِمَا كَسَبُواْ مَا تَرَكَ عَلَىٰ ظَهۡرِهَا مِن دَآبَّةٖ\nIbn Masoud said: The beetle is almost punished in his hole because of the sins of the son of Adam. Yahya bin Abi Kathir said: A man enjoined what is right and prohibited what is evil, so, another man said to him: Take care of your own self, as the wrongdoer does not harm but himself. Abu Huraira replied: You lied, by Allah, other than whom there is no god; then said: By Him, in Whose Hand my soul is, the bustard dies of hunger in its nest due to the wrongdoer’s action. Al-Qurtubi: 17/401-402.\nDo the sins of people have effects on animals?\nوَلَوۡ يُؤَاخِذُ ٱللَّهُ ٱلنَّاسَ بِمَا كَسَبُواْ مَا تَرَكَ عَلَىٰ ظَهۡرِهَا مِن دَآبَّةٖ وَلَٰكِن يُؤَخِّرُهُمۡ إِلَىٰٓ أَجَلٖ مُّسَمّٗىۖ فَإِذَا جَآءَ أَجَلُهُمۡ فَإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ كَانَ بِعِبَادِهِۦ بَصِيرَۢا ٤٥\nThis is a reminder to them that they should not misconstrue the respite as an inability to punish them, or contentment of what they are doing; after all, it was they who said: (O Allah, if this is indeed the truth from You, then rain down upon us stones from the heaven or bring upon us a painful punishment) [8:32]. Allah informs them that the timing of His punishment is tied to His wisdom that takes into account the interests of other nations, or the preservation of the next generations. Ibn Ashur: 22/239.\nDelaying the punishment of the polytheists is not a sign of their true ways. How does this verse show this meaning?\nوَٱلۡقُرۡءَانِ ٱلۡحَكِيمِ ٢ إِنَّكَ لَمِنَ ٱلۡمُرۡسَلِينَ ٣\nIndeed the holy Quran is the strongest evidence that has remained down throughout the ages, of the truth of the message of the Messenger (ﷺ). All the evidence of the Quran is evidence that supports the message of Muhammad (ﷺ). Al-Saadi: 692.\nWhat is the strongest evidence of the Prophet’s (ﷺ) Message?\nتَنزِيلَ ٱلۡعَزِيزِ ٱلرَّحِيمِ ٥\nAllah protected it by His might from change and alteration, and by means of it He granted mercy to His servants that would stay with them until it brings them to the realm of His mercy. Hence the verse ends with these two divine honorable names, (the Almighty, the Most Merciful). Al-Saadi: 692.\nThe verse ends with these two Holy Names, (the All-Mighty) and (Most Merciful). Why?\nإِنَّمَا تُنذِرُ مَنِ ٱتَّبَعَ ٱلذِّكۡرَ وَخَشِيَ ٱلرَّحۡمَٰنَ بِٱلۡغَيۡبِۖ فَبَشِّرۡهُ بِمَغۡفِرَةٖ وَأَجۡرٖ كَرِيمٍ ١١\nMeaning: Allah has given us this position and status out of His grace, blessing, and mercy, for our good deeds were not equivalent to this. Ibn Kathir: 3/535.\nCan a person enter Paradise based solely on his deeds? Explain in light of this verse.\nإِنَّا نَحۡنُ نُحۡيِ ٱلۡمَوۡتَىٰ وَنَكۡتُبُ مَا قَدَّمُواْ وَءَاثَٰرَهُمۡۚ وَكُلَّ شَيۡءٍ أَحۡصَيۡنَٰهُ فِيٓ إِمَامٖ مُّبِينٖ ١٢\nThe legacy left behind by man, whether it is good or evil, will be recompensed for it. A good legacy such as taught knowledge, or written book. A bad legacy, such as a position of authority given by him to a wrongdoer, or a distraction that turned people away from the remembrance of Allah. this applies to every good or bad deed that is emulated by others. Al-Qurtubi: 17/420.\nIt is important that you leave a good legacy after your death. Why? What is the consequence of leaving a bad legacy?\nإِنَّا نَحۡنُ نُحۡيِ ٱلۡمَوۡتَىٰ وَنَكۡتُبُ مَا قَدَّمُواْ وَءَاثَٰرَهُمۡۚ\nThis refers to their legacy of good or evil, of which they were the cause during their lifetimes and after their deaths. This highlights the high status of one who calls people to Allah and guides them to His path by all possible means, and the low status of one who calls people to evil and leads others therein; the latter is one of the worst of people, who is guilty of the worst crime and gravest sin. Al-Saadi: 693.\nGiven this verse, explain the status of one who calls people to Allah.\nwords\nفِي أَعنَاقِهِم أَغلاَلًاTheir hands were tied to their necks; due to their persistence in disbelief\nمُقمَحُونَTheir heads are forced to remain up\nفَأَغشَينَاهُمWe blocked their vision\nوَآثَارَهُمWhat they left behind; good and evil"],[441,"§Ya-Sin\ndeeds\nFin a group of people who are heedless of performing the daily prayers and advise them to do so.\nShow support to one of the righteous or preachers by spreading his virtue and biography through messages or any other means.\nAbsolve yourself before Allah by enjoining what is right, or prohibiting what is wrong.\nguid\nFollow the footsteps of the Messengers.\nDo not ask for a recompense for calling others to Allah, as it is one of the reasons for being accepted.\nRejoice over the guidance of people, not over their punishment, for it is the best quality a pious preacher can have.\nrefl\nوَٱضۡرِبۡ لَهُم مَّثَلًا أَصۡحَٰبَ ٱلۡقَرۡيَةِ\nIf there was any benefit in identifying the city in question, Allah would have identified it. You should realize that the path to sound knowledge is to be content with the facts and turn away from discussing what is of no benefit. Thus, the seeker of knowledge will maintain purity of heart and his knowledge will increase. This is in contrast to the ignorant person who thinks that his knowledge will increase by referring to views and ideas that have no basis or proof, and are of no benefit, and in fact, they only lead to confusion and distraction, and leave one open to accepting doubtful matters. Al-Saadi: 693.\nWhat is the ideal way of dealing with the indefinite things in the Quran?\nقَالُواْ طَٰٓئِرُكُم مَّعَكُمۡ أَئِن ذُكِّرۡتُمۚ بَلۡ أَنتُمۡ قَوۡمٞ مُّسۡرِفُونَ ١٩\n(Your bad omen is with yourselves), your luck, whether good or bad, is with you because of your actions and deeds; it is not because of us, rather, it is due to your transgression and disbelief. Most interpreters agree with this interpretation. Ibn Atiyah: 4/450.\nThis verse responds to those who consider something or someone a bad omen. Explain.\nوَجَآءَ مِنۡ أَقۡصَا ٱلۡمَدِينَةِ رَجُلٞ يَسۡعَىٰ قَالَ يَٰقَوۡمِ ٱتَّبِعُواْ ٱلۡمُرۡسَلِينَ ٢٠\nDescribing the man as (rushing) indicates that he came in a hurry; he was informed that people of the city were going to stone or torment the Messengers, so, he wanted to advise them for fear for them and the Messengers. This is praise for him to have set an example to follow in rushing to change what was evil. Ibn Ashur: 22/366.\nWhat does the word (rushing) indicate?\nوَجَآءَ مِنۡ أَقۡصَا ٱلۡمَدِينَةِ رَجُلٞ يَسۡعَىٰ قَالَ يَٰقَوۡمِ ٱتَّبِعُواْ ٱلۡمُرۡسَلِينَ ٢٠\nThe expression (from the farthest end of the city) precedes the word (a man) in order to emphasize the praise for those who live in the outskirt the city. More good may be found at the outskirts of the city than at its center. The humble people who live outside the city are among the first to accept the faith, unlike the chiefs who live in a great luxury at the center of the city. Ibn Ashur: 22/365.\nThe expression (from the farthest end of the city) precedes the word (a man). Why?\nٱتَّبِعُواْ مَن لَّا يَسۡـَٔلُكُمۡ أَجۡرٗا وَهُم مُّهۡتَدُونَ ٢١\nMeaning: Those Messengers do not ask you for a payment for calling you to the faith, hence, you will not lose anything of your worldly possessions, rather, you will be rightly guided. Ibn Juzay: 2/222.\nThis verse mentions two factors indicating the truthfulness of the preacher. What are they?\nٱتَّبِعُواْ مَن لَّا يَسۡـَٔلُكُمۡ أَجۡرٗا وَهُم مُّهۡتَدُونَ ٢١\n(Follow those who ask no recompense of you), follow those who give you advice that will bring you good, and who do not want your wealth or any recompense for advising you and guiding you, for this makes it incumbent upon you to follow those who are like that. There is only one argument left, which is the idea that perhaps a Messenger may call people and not ask any recompense for that, but he is not calling to the truth. So, he warded off this notion by saying: (And who are rightly guided), because they were only calling to something of which sound reason testifies to its beauty and goodness, and they were not forbidding anything of which sound reason does not testify to its ugliness. Al-Saadi: 694.\nThe verse ends with (and who are rightly guided). Why?\nقِيلَ ٱدۡخُلِ ٱلۡجَنَّةَۖ قَالَ يَٰلَيۡتَ قَوۡمِي يَعۡلَمُونَ ٢٦ بِمَا غَفَرَ لِي رَبِّي وَجَعَلَنِي مِنَ ٱلۡمُكۡرَمِينَ ٢٧\nThis verse emphasizes the importance of restraining anger, and showing forbearance toward ignorant people. Being kind to those who joined evil company, and engaging in trying to rid them of that instead of rejoicing over their problems or invoking Allah against them. Do you see how he wished good for his killers who were disbelievers and idols worshipers. Al-Qurtubi: 17/433.\nWhat is the great quality that the believer learns from this verse?\nwords\nفَعَزَّزنَاWe supported and strengthened\nتَطَيَّرنَا بِكُمWe consider you a bad omen\nطَائِرُكُم مَعَكُمYour omen is with yourselves\nأَئِن ذُكِّرتُمIs it because you were reminded\nيَسعَىCame rushing\nفَطَرَنِيWho created me"],[442,"§Ya-Sin\ndeeds\nRead one of the Prophets' stories in the Quran, and reflect on the destruction of their people such as Pharaohs, Aad, or others.\nReflect on some of the grains and fruits in your food - who grew them until they reach you, then thank Allah for His countless blessings.\nIn the morning, say, \"O Allah, by You the morning enters upon us and by You the evening enters upon us, and by You we live and by You we die and to You is the resurrection.\" And in the evening, say, \"O Allah, by You the evening enters upon us and by You the morning enters upon us, and by You we live and by You we die and to You is the return.\"\nguid\nAllah's punishment of those who disobeyed Him was very intense, where He destroyed them with a single blast.\nReflect on the Day when all the creations are brought to stand before Allah, the Almighty.\nReflect on the creations of Allah; the earth and its crops, and heaven and its planets.\nrefl\n۞وَمَآ أَنزَلۡنَا عَلَىٰ قَوۡمِهِۦ مِنۢ بَعۡدِهِۦ مِن جُندٖ مِّنَ ٱلسَّمَآءِ وَمَا كُنَّا مُنزِلِينَ ٢٨\nMeaning: Allah has destroyed them with a single blast by the angel Gabriel, and He did not need to send down soldiers from heaven to punish them because they were insignificant. Ibn Juzay: 2/223.\nGiven this verse, describe the weakness and insignificance of nations when Allah wants to punish them.\n۞وَمَآ أَنزَلۡنَا عَلَىٰ قَوۡمِهِۦ مِنۢ بَعۡدِهِۦ مِن جُندٖ مِّنَ ٱلسَّمَآءِ وَمَا كُنَّا مُنزِلِينَ ٢٨\nMeaning: We did not need to go to the trouble of punishing them by sending down troops from heaven to destroy them (nor would We have done so) because of the great might of Allah and the extreme weakness of human beings, the slightest touch of divine punishment that befalls them is sufficient. Al-Saadi: 695.\nDescribe the weakness of mankind in light of this verse.\nيَٰحَسۡرَةً عَلَى ٱلۡعِبَادِۚ مَا يَأۡتِيهِم مِّن رَّسُولٍ إِلَّا كَانُواْ بِهِۦ يَسۡتَهۡزِءُونَ ٣٠\nHow regretful the servants will be for themselves, how sorry and grievous they will be for ridiculing Allah's Messengers (p). Al-Qurtubi: 17/436.\nWhat is the reason for the servants' regret?\nوَءَايَةٞ لَّهُمُ ٱلۡأَرۡضُ ٱلۡمَيۡتَةُ أَحۡيَيۡنَٰهَا وَأَخۡرَجۡنَا مِنۡهَا حَبّٗا فَمِنۡهُ يَأۡكُلُونَ ٣٣\nAllah brought the dead earth to life by growing its plants and grains as a sign for them to direct their attention to His power of giving life to the dead, and to remind them of His Oneness and absolute power. Al-Qurtubi: 17/44.\nWhat is the benefit of mentioning the revival of the dead earth at this stage?\nسُبۡحَٰنَ ٱلَّذِي خَلَقَ ٱلۡأَزۡوَٰجَ كُلَّهَا مِمَّا تُنۢبِتُ ٱلۡأَرۡضُ وَمِنۡ أَنفُسِهِمۡ وَمِمَّا لَا يَعۡلَمُونَ ٣٦\nMeaning: How odd is the persistence of those disbelievers on their disbelief despite all the signs that they witness; and whoever wonders at something, says, \"Glory be to Allah.\" Al-Qurtubi: 17/441.\nWhat should one say when he wonders at something?\nوَءَايَةٞ لَّهُمُ ٱلَّيۡلُ نَسۡلَخُ مِنۡهُ ٱلنَّهَارَ فَإِذَا هُم مُّظۡلِمُونَ ٣٧ وَٱلشَّمۡسُ تَجۡرِي لِمُسۡتَقَرّٖ لَّهَاۚ ذَٰلِكَ تَقۡدِيرُ ٱلۡعَزِيزِ ٱلۡعَلِيمِ ٣٨ وَٱلۡقَمَرَ قَدَّرۡنَٰهُ مَنَازِلَ حَتَّىٰ عَادَ كَٱلۡعُرۡجُونِ ٱلۡقَدِيمِ ٣٩ لَا ٱلشَّمۡسُ يَنۢبَغِي لَهَآ أَن تُدۡرِكَ ٱلۡقَمَرَ وَلَا ٱلَّيۡلُ سَابِقُ ٱلنَّهَارِۚ وَكُلّٞ فِي فَلَكٖ يَسۡبَحُونَ ٤٠\nAll of this offers clear evidence and proof for the greatness of the Creator and the sublime nature of His Attributes, especially His might, wisdom, and knowledge in this context. Al-Saadi: 696.\nWhat are the divine attributes inferred from these verses?\nوَٱلشَّمۡسُ تَجۡرِي لِمُسۡتَقَرّٖ لَّهَاۚ ذَٰلِكَ تَقۡدِيرُ ٱلۡعَزِيزِ ٱلۡعَلِيمِ ٣٨\nThese two attributes (The All-Mighty, the All-Knowing) are mentioned because they pertain to the planets movement system, where the His might pertains to the subjugation of this great universe, and His knowledge pertains to the precision of this innovative system. Ibn Ashur: 23/21.\nThe verse ends with these two attributes (the All-Mighty, the All-Knowing). Why?\nwords\nخَامِدُونَThey were extinguished\nمُحضَرُونَThey will be brought for reckoning\nنَسلَخُWe strip\nكَالعُرجُونِ القَدِيمِLike an old dried curved date stalk\nيَسبَحُونَThey float, move"],[443,"§Ya-Sin\ndeeds\nConsider if there were no modern means of transportation, how would your suffering be like? Then thank Allah, the Almighty, for giving it to us.\nAsk Allah humbly and say, \"O Allah, I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your wrath, and I seek refuge in Your forgiveness from Your punishment.\"\nGive charity to the poor or the needy.\nguid\nOne of the signs of mankind’s weakness is that they needed only one ship to survive during the time of Noah (u).\nOnly Allah's mercy can save the servant from punishment in worldly life and the Hereafter.\nIf you hear a verse or a sermon, take it with your heart and do what it says .\nrefl\nوَءَايَةٞ لَّهُمۡ أَنَّا حَمَلۡنَا ذُرِّيَّتَهُمۡ فِي ٱلۡفُلۡكِ ٱلۡمَشۡحُونِ ٤١\nThe offspring were mentioned because of their weakness for travel, and therefore, the blessing of carrying them is apparent. Ibn Atiyah: 4/455.\nWhy is the offspring mentioned in this verse?\nمَا يَنظُرُونَ إِلَّا صَيۡحَةٗ وَٰحِدَةٗ تَأۡخُذُهُمۡ وَهُمۡ يَخِصِّمُونَ ٤٩\n(While they are still disputing), while they are distracted from it, and it never crosses their minds while they are disputing and arguing with one another, which usually happens when they are heedless. Al-Saadi: 697.\nOf all the times, the disputing time is singled out for mention. Why?\nمَا يَنظُرُونَ إِلَّا صَيۡحَةٗ وَٰحِدَةٗ تَأۡخُذُهُمۡ وَهُمۡ يَخِصِّمُونَ ٤٩\nMeaning: They will dispute over their worldly affairs such as selling and buying, and they will be talking in homes and markets. Al-Baghawi: 3/643.\nDescribe the state of people’s heedlessness when the Day of Resurrection starts.\nفَلَا يَسۡتَطِيعُونَ تَوۡصِيَةٗ وَلَآ إِلَىٰٓ أَهۡلِهِمۡ يَرۡجِعُونَ ٥٠\nThe household [family] are mentioned because speaking to them at that time is more important and assured than speaking to others. Ibn Atiyah: 4/457.\nThe household [family] are specified in this verse for a reason. What is it?\nقَالُواْ يَٰوَيۡلَنَا مَنۢ بَعَثَنَا مِن مَّرۡقَدِنَاۜ هَٰذَا مَا وَعَدَ ٱلرَّحۡمَٰنُ وَصَدَقَ ٱلۡمُرۡسَلُونَ ٥٢\nIt is said: When the disbelievers say to each other: (Who has raised us up from our sleeping place), they will believe the Messengers after they see what they told them, hence, the disbelievers will say: (This is what the Most Merciful had promised, and the messengers told the truth), but we denied it. They will then admit to their guilt but to no avail. Al-Qurtubi: 17/465.\nWhen will the disbelievers show regret for their disbelief?\nقَالُواْ يَٰوَيۡلَنَا مَنۢ بَعَثَنَا مِن مَّرۡقَدِنَاۜ\nMeaning: Their graves, which in this world they thought they would never be raised from. When they see with their own eyes that in which they had disbelieved, (They will say: \"Woe to us! Who has raised us up from our sleeping place\"). This does not contradict the fact that they will be punished in their graves, because in comparison to what is to come afterwards, that will seem like taking a nap. Ibn Kathir: 3/552.\nDoes the polytheists’ saying: (Who has raised us up from our sleeping place) contradict the punishment in their grave?\nهَٰذَا مَا وَعَدَ ٱلرَّحۡمَٰنُ وَصَدَقَ ٱلۡمُرۡسَلُونَ ٥٢\nDo not think that mention of the divine name, the Most Merciful, in this context is merely because it is speaking of His promise. Rather, it highlights the fact that on that momentous day, they will see of His mercy which never crossed their minds and no one expected. This is like the verses in which Allah says: (On that day true dominion will belong to the Most Merciful) [25:26], and (All voices will be stilled before the Most Merciful) [20:108]. And other similar verses, in which the divine name (the Most Merciful) is mentioned in this context. Al-Saadi: 697.\nThe divine name, (the Most Merciful) is specified in this context. Why?\nwords\nفَلاَ صَرِيخَNo rescuer\nيَخِصِّمُونَThey will dispute in their worldly affairs\nالأَجدَاثِGraves\nيَنسِلُونَThey will rush\nمَرقَدِنَاOur sleeping place"],[444,"§Ya-Sin\ndeeds\nSay, \"O Allah, I ask you for the eternal bliss.\"\nDo a good physical deed, such as helping a Muslim, or removing harm from the road.\nSay, \"O Allah, I seek refuge with You from reaching a degraded geriatric old age, and I seek refuge with You from being led astray by the devil at the time of my death.\"\nguid\nThe companions of Paradise will be preoccupied with bliss as a recompense for their preoccupation with worships in worldly life.\nStudy and recite verses from the Book of Allah, for it gives life to the heart.\nDo not be immersed in poetry and songs, lest it distracts you from the Holy Quran.\nrefl\nإِنَّ أَصۡحَٰبَ ٱلۡجَنَّةِ ٱلۡيَوۡمَ فِي شُغُلٖ فَٰكِهُونَ ٥٥\nThis indicates that the companions of Paradise will be hastened to its bliss before the companions of Hellfire are taken to it, and so the companions of Paradise will not witness that sight. Ibn Ashur: 23/4.\nThis verse infers that Allah will honor the companions of Paradise by hastening them to it. How?\nوَٱمۡتَٰزُواْ ٱلۡيَوۡمَ أَيُّهَا ٱلۡمُجۡرِمُونَ ٥٩\nMuqatil said: \"Distance yourselves from the righteous ones today.\" Ad-Dahhak said: \"There is a house in Hellfire for every disbeliever; he will enter it, and its door will be sealed by fire, where he will remain therein for eternity.\" Al-Baghawi: 3/645.\nHow will the criminals stand apart from the people of faith on the Day of Resurrection?\n۞أَلَمۡ أَعۡهَدۡ إِلَيۡكُمۡ يَٰبَنِيٓ ءَادَمَ أَن لَّا تَعۡبُدُواْ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنَۖ إِنَّهُۥ لَكُمۡ عَدُوّٞ مُّبِينٞ ٦٠\nThis rebuke is for all kinds of disbelief and sins, because all of it is obedience to satan and worship of him. Al-Saadi: 698.\nWhat is included in the rebuke mentioned in this verse?\nٱلۡيَوۡمَ نَخۡتِمُ عَلَىٰٓ أَفۡوَٰهِهِمۡ وَتُكَلِّمُنَآ أَيۡدِيهِمۡ وَتَشۡهَدُ أَرۡجُلُهُم بِمَا كَانُواْ يَكۡسِبُونَ ٦٥\nIt is said that since the hands do the action while the feet witness it, then, the statement of the witness is a testimony, and the statement of the perpetrator against himself is admission. That is why the hands will speak and the feet will testify, as expressed in the verse. Al-Qurtubi: 17/476.\nThe verse mentions that the hands will speak and the feet will testify. Why?\nوَمَن نُّعَمِّرۡهُ نُنَكِّسۡهُ فِي ٱلۡخَلۡقِۚ\nAllah makes clear that the longer the son of Adam lives, the weaker he becomes after being strong, and incapable after being able and active. The meaning here -and Allah knows best- is that Allah informs us that this world is transient and will come to an end; it is not eternal or lasting. Ibn Kathir: 3/555.\nWhat is the aim of informing about the reversal of man’s abilities when he gets older?\nوَمَا عَلَّمۡنَٰهُ ٱلشِّعۡرَ وَمَا يَنۢبَغِي لَهُۥٓۚ إِنۡ هُوَ إِلَّا ذِكۡرٞ وَقُرۡءَانٞ مُّبِينٞ ٦٩\nIbn Al-Qasim narrated that Imam Malik was asked about reciting poems, and he replied: \"Do not do it often, for Allah says, (And We have not taught him poetry, nor is it fitting for him).\" Al-Qurtubi: 17/484.\nIs reciting poetry often a good thing? What is the proof for that?\nلِّيُنذِرَ مَن كَانَ حَيّٗا وَيَحِقَّ ٱلۡقَوۡلُ عَلَى ٱلۡكَٰفِرِينَ ٧٠\nThe Quran warns (whoever is alive), a believer whose heart is alive, because the disbeliever is like the dead who does not reflect nor ponders. Al-Baghawi: 3/649.\nWho is meant by the alive and dead in this verse?\nwords\nالأَرَائِكِAdorned couches\nوَامتَازُواStand apart from the believers\nلَمَسَخنَاهُمWe could deform them\nمَكَانَتِهِمTheir places\nمُضِيًّاTo proceed ahead\nنُعَمِّرهُWhom We grant long life\nنُنَكِّسهُ فِي الخَلقِWe reverse him back to his weak state"],[445,"§Ya-Sin\ndeeds\nShow your gratitude for Allah's favors: Riding, eating, drinking and clothing.\nSay, \"O Allah, do not abandon me to myself even for a blink of an eye, nor less than that.\"\nSay, \"O Allah, help me and do not give help against me; grant me victory and do not grant victory over me; guide me and make right guidance easy for me.\"\nguid\nSeek only Allah's help for all of your needs.\nReflect on the origins of your creation so you know the limits of your ability.\nNever argue or dispute anything for the sake of obstinacy and rejecting truth.\nrefl\nأَوَ لَمۡ يَرَوۡاْ أَنَّا خَلَقۡنَا لَهُم مِّمَّا عَمِلَتۡ أَيۡدِينَآ أَنۡعَٰمٗا فَهُمۡ لَهَا مَٰلِكُونَ مَٰلِكُونَ ٧١\nThey are their owners), Allah created these animals (grazing livestock), and made them subservient to mankind so, they are able to control and dominate them. Al-Baghawi: 3/649.\nAllah bestows upon mankind the grazing livestock and makes them subservient. Why?\nوَلَهُمۡ فِيهَا مَنَٰفِعُ وَمَشَارِبُۚ أَفَلَا يَشۡكُرُونَ ٧٣\n(So will they not be grateful?), this is an interrogative and exclamatory sentence about them for not being continually grateful for these abundant favors. The present tense in the verse indicates that these favors are renewed continuously by Allah at all times. Ibn Ashur: 23/69.\nThis verse indicates the importance of being always grateful for the favors of Allah. How?\nفَلَا يَحۡزُنكَ قَوۡلُهُمۡۘ إِنَّا نَعۡلَمُ مَا يُسِرُّونَ وَمَا يُعۡلِنُونَ ٧٦\nMeaning: We know that what incites them to say that is envy. They know in their hearts that what you are reciting is not a poem and that you are not a liar. We know that they conceal the knowledge that you came with the truth, and we know what they reveal by their tongues of proclaiming disbelief. Al-Tabari:20/553.\nFor one who calls people to Allah, how can he benefit from this verse?\nإِنَّا نَعۡلَمُ مَا يُسِرُّونَ وَمَا يُعۡلِنُونَ ٧٦\nMeaning: We know everything about them, and We will punish them for their false claims and deal with them accordingly on the Day when none of their deeds, great or small, major or minor, will be overlooked, and every deed they did throughout their worldly lives will be exposed. Ibn Kathir: 3/558.\nAllah asserts that He Knows what the disbelievers conceal and reveal. Why?\nقُلۡ يُحۡيِيهَا ٱلَّذِيٓ أَنشَأَهَآ أَوَّلَ مَرَّةٖۖ وَهُوَ بِكُلِّ خَلۡقٍ عَلِيمٌ ٧٩\nHe knows about the bones in all areas and regions of the earth; where they have gone, where they disintegrated and dispersed. Ibn Kathir: 3/559.\nGiven this verse, describe the limitless knowledge of Allah.\nٱلَّذِي جَعَلَ لَكُم مِّنَ ٱلشَّجَرِ ٱلۡأَخۡضَرِ نَارٗا فَإِذَآ أَنتُم مِّنۡهُ تُوقِدُونَ ٨٠\nThen, Allah mentions a third proof, (The One who made for you from the green tree, fire, and then from it you ignite). If He produces fire, which is dry, from the green trees, which are very damp and moist, even though their characteristics are diametrically opposed, then His bringing forth of the dead from their graves is akin to that. Al-Saadi: 700.\nHow can we infer the resurrection of the dead from this verse?\nفَسُبۡحَٰنَ ٱلَّذِي بِيَدِهِۦ مَلَكُوتُ كُلِّ شَيۡءٖ وَإِلَيۡهِ تُرۡجَعُونَ ٨٣\nThey did not revere Allah with His true reverence, and everyone who denied the resurrection of the dead had done so because of his ignorance of the supreme power of Allah. Ibn Juzay: 2/230.\nWhat is the reason for the disbelievers' denial of the resurrection of the dead?\nwords\nوَذَلَّلنَاهَاMade them subservient\nرَكُوبُهُمSome they ride in their travel\nخَصِيمٌAdversary\nرَمِيمٌCrumbled to dust"],[446,"§As-Saffat\ndeeds\nReflect on the creation of the stars, then thank Allah for preventing the devils from eavesdropping, lest they mislead people.\nSeek refuge with Allah from the evil of the accursed satan.\nRecall a piece of advice that you have heard and hasten to follow it.\nguid\nReflect on the situation of the devils and their repellence after the Message of Muhammad's (ﷺ).\nDo not be among those who do not remember when reminded.\nWatch your words and actions, in order that you will not be in a terrible position before Allah.\nrefl\nوَٱلصَّٰٓفَّٰتِ صَفّٗا ١\nThe angels line up in rows in heaven like the people on earth line up for the prayer. Moreover, it is said the angels spread out their wings in heaven and keep still until Allah commands them of what He wills. Al-Qurtubi: 18/6.\nHow do the angels show humility and submission to Allah?\nإِنَّ إِلَٰهَكُمۡ لَوَٰحِدٞ ٤ رَّبُّ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِ وَمَا بَيۡنَهُمَا وَرَبُّ ٱلۡمَشَٰرِقِ ٥\nMeaning: He is the Creator of these things, Who provides for them and controls them; just as He has no partner in His Lordship over them, so too He has no partner in His divinity. Allah often affirms the Oneness of His divinity by affirming the Oneness of His Lordship, because it is indicative of it, and the polytheists themselves also affirmed it, so, He proves to them the soundness of what they denied on the basis of what they affirm. Al-Saadi: 700.\nAllah mentions the Oneness of His Lordship after the Oneness of His divinity. Why?\nإِنَّا زَيَّنَّا ٱلسَّمَآءَ ٱلدُّنۡيَا بِزِينَةٍ ٱلۡكَوَاكِبِ ٦\nAllah singles out the nearest heaven for mention because it is within our vision range, and the fact that the protection from devils is confined to it. Ibn Atiyah: 4/466.\nAllah singles out the nearest heaven for mention for two reasons. What are they?\nبَلۡ عَجِبۡتَ وَيَسۡخَرُونَ ١٢\nQatadah said: The Prophet (ﷺ) was astonished at the misguidance of the sons of Adam after the revelation of the Quran; that was because the Prophet (ﷺ) thought that whoever hears the Quran, will believe in it, but when the polytheists heard the Quran, they ridiculed it and did not believe in it, so he was astonished at that. Al-Baghawi: 3/656.\nWhat prompted the Prophet's (ﷺ) astonishment at the disbelief in the Quran by the polytheists?\nقُلۡ نَعَمۡ وَأَنتُمۡ دَٰخِرُونَ ١٨\nThey will become humiliated and disdained because when they see what they have denied, they will inevitably become disgraced. Al-Qurtubi: 18/22.\nWhat is the cause of the disgrace of disobedient people on the Day of Resurrection?\n۞ٱحۡشُرُواْ ٱلَّذِينَ ظَلَمُواْ وَأَزۡوَٰجَهُمۡ وَمَا كَانُواْ يَعۡبُدُونَ ٢٢ مِن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ فَٱهۡدُوهُمۡ إِلَىٰ صِرَٰطِ ٱلۡجَحِيمِ ٢٣\nGather them to stand for reckoning and recompense. (And their fellows): Their followers and the likes of them. Qatadah and Al-Kalbi said: All those who had done the same as the wrongdoers did; so, the people who drank intoxicants will be together, and the people who committed adultery will be together. Al-Baghawi: 3/657.\nWhat will be the company of the person on the Day of Resurrection? What do we learn from that?\nوَقِفُوهُمۡۖ إِنَّهُم مَّسۡـُٔولُونَ ٢٤\nWhen they are driven to Hellfire, they will be stopped at the bridge set over it, and will it be said: (Stop them; indeed, they are to be questioned). Ibn Abbas said: They will be questioned about all of their words and actions. Al-Baghawi: 3/657.\nWhere will they be stopped before Allah? What will they be questioned about on the Day of Resurrection?\nwords\nوَالصَّآفَّاتِAn oath by the angels who lined up in rows\nفَالزَّاجِرَاتِAn oath by the angels who drive the clouds\nفَالتَّالِيَاتِ ذِكرًاAn oath by the angels who recite Allah’s words\nمَارِدٍA rebellious devil\nدُحُورًاDevils who are repelled away from listening\nوَاصِبٌA perpetual and painful\nخَطِفَ الخَطفَةَA devil who snatches away some words\nلاَزِبٍA sticky clay"],[447,"§As-Saffat\ndeeds\nVisit a Muslim brother for the sake of Allah.\nWrite a message in defense of someone who invites others to Allah.\nToday, say often, \"None has the right to be worshiped except Allah.\"\nguid\nKeep the company of righteous people, and abandon others.\nBeware of following misguiding leaders and their whims because they will turn into enemies on the Day of Resurrection.\nHumble yourself to the truth, and desist from arrogance.\nrefl\nمَا لَكُمۡ لَا تَنَاصَرُونَ ٢٥\nIt is as if they will not answer this question, because they will be overcome with humiliation and shame; they will surrender to the punishment of the Fire and will become submissive, having lost all hope, so they will not speak. Al-Saadi: 702.\nAllah mentions questioning the people of the Fire, but not their answer. Why?\nفَإِنَّهُمۡ يَوۡمَئِذٖ فِي ٱلۡعَذَابِ مُشۡتَرِكُونَ ٣٣ إِنَّا كَذَٰلِكَ نَفۡعَلُ بِٱلۡمُجۡرِمِينَ ٣٤\nMeaning: This is how We treat those who, in this world, had chosen disobedience to Allah over His obedience, and disbelief in Him over accepting faith in Him. Hence, We make them taste the painful punishment, and gather them with their companions in the Fire. Al-Tabari: 21/33.\nAssociation and likeness in this world lead to association in the Hereafter. How?\nأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ لَهُمۡ رِزۡقٞ مَّعۡلُومٞ ٤١ فَوَٰكِهُ وَهُم مُّكۡرَمُونَ ٤٢ فِي جَنَّٰتِ ٱلنَّعِيمِ ٤٣ عَلَىٰ سُرُرٖ مُّتَقَٰبِلِينَ ٤٤ يُطَافُ عَلَيۡهِم بِكَأۡسٖ مِّن مَّعِينِۢ ٤٥ بَيۡضَآءَ لَذَّةٖ لِّلشَّٰرِبِينَ ٤٦ لَا فِيهَا غَوۡلٞ وَلَا هُمۡ عَنۡهَا يُنزَفُونَ ٤٧ وَعِندَهُمۡ قَٰصِرَٰتُ ٱلطَّرۡفِ عِينٞ ٤٨ كَأَنَّهُنَّ بَيۡضٞ مَّكۡنُونٞ ٤٩\nAllah describes their food, drinks, places to sit, and the overall bliss, the details of which are included in this verse, (in Gardens of Bliss), however, He details these things so they will be known, and the souls will long for them. Al-Saadi: 703.\nAllah details the bliss of the people of Paradise even though this verse (in Gardens of Bliss) is inclusive. Why?\nفَوَٰكِهُ وَهُم مُّكۡرَمُونَ ٤٢ فِي جَنَّٰتِ ٱلنَّعِيمِ ٤٣\nAllah will honor them by raising high their ranks and enabling them to hear and see Him. Al-Qurtubi: 18/29.\nDescribe some of the honor bestowed by Allah upon His sincere servants.\nلَا فِيهَا غَوۡلٞ وَلَا هُمۡ عَنۡهَا يُنزَفُونَ ٤٧\nMeaning: The wine of Paradise will not distort their minds, and they will not suffer sickness or headache. Allah has averted intoxication from the people of Paradise, lest they cease to enjoy the pleasures of Paradise. Al-Qurtubi: 18/31-33.\nAllah has averted intoxication from the people of Paradise. Why?\nوَعِندَهُمۡ قَٰصِرَٰتُ ٱلطَّرۡفِ عِينٞ ٤٨\nWhat is meant is either that this beautiful and chaste woman restrains her glance and looks only at her husband, because of her chastity, and she does not look beyond him to anyone else, and because of the perfection and beauty of her husband, which is such that she does not want anyone else in paradise but him. All of this is indicative of the beauty of men. Al-Saadi: 703.\nThis verse indicates the beauty of men in Paradise. How?\nفَأَقۡبَلَ بَعۡضُهُمۡ عَلَىٰ بَعۡضٖ يَتَسَآءَلُونَ ٥٠ قَالَ قَآئِلٞ مِّنۡهُمۡ إِنِّي كَانَ لِي قَرِينٞ ٥١\nIt is well known that people of knowledge find joy in raising questions about issues and researching matters, and that joy is greater than the pleasure that other people find in discussing worldly matters. So, they will have an abundant share of this kind of joy, and they will attain the discovery of some facts in paradise that cannot be expressed. Al-Saadi: 704.\nPeople of knowledge will find special joy in Paradise through conversing. What is it?\nwords\nعَنِ اليَمِينِFrom the side of the truth and religion\nسُلطَانٍProof, authority\nطَاغِينَA transgressing people\nفَحَقَّ عَلَينَاIt has come into effect upon us\nالمُخلَصِينَThose who are sincere, and Allah chose them for His mercy\nلاَ فِيهَا غَولٌNo bad effect is there in it\nوَلاَ هُم عَنهَا يُنزَفُونَNor from it will they be intoxicated\nمَكنُونٌProtected, untouched\nقَرِينٌA close friend"],[448,"§As-Saffat\ndeeds\nHelp your mother with her chores for the day.\nFast a day for the sake of Allah to be saved from the scorching heat of Resurrection Day.\nCall on Allah, the Almighty, in humbleness.\nguid\nA good friend is better than dozens of heedless ones.\nDo not wrong anyone, for the tree of Zaqqum is the punishment of the wrongdoers.\nKnow that no one responds to prayers but Allah and no succorer but Him.\nrefl\nفَٱطَّلَعَ فَرَءَاهُ فِي سَوَآءِ ٱلۡجَحِيمِ ٥٥ قَالَ تَٱللَّهِ إِن كِدتَّ لَتُرۡدِينِ ٥٦ وَلَوۡلَا نِعۡمَةُ رَبِّي لَكُنتُ مِنَ ٱلۡمُحۡضَرِينَ ٥٧\nThis verse presents a lesson for people to avoid evil companions and beware of the misdeeds that they call others to, and make them appealing to them. Ibn Ashur: 23/119.\nGiven this verse, describe the risk of having an evil companion.\nفَٱطَّلَعَ فَرَءَاهُ فِي سَوَآءِ ٱلۡجَحِيمِ ٥٥\nSome scholars said: If Allah, the Almighty, will not make him recognizable to him, he will not be able to know who he is, because his color and shape will have changed. Al-Qurtubi: 18/39.\nHow will someone in Paradise recognize his old companion who is in the Fire after his color and shape is changed?\nوَلَوۡلَا نِعۡمَةُ رَبِّي لَكُنتُ مِنَ ٱلۡمُحۡضَرِينَ ٥٧\n(If not for the favor of my Lord): His mercy and favor upon me for being a Muslim. (I would have been of those brought in): With you in Hellfire. Al-Baghawi: 3/661.\nWhen the believer is saved from Hellfire, is that due to his deeds and obedience only?\nإِنَّهَا شَجَرَةٞ تَخۡرُجُ فِيٓ أَصۡلِ ٱلۡجَحِيمِ ٦٤\nThat is where this tree emerges, and the substance of which it is made is the worst of substances. The vileness of the place where it grows is indicative of how vile and foul this plant is. Hence, Allah draws our attention to its vile nature by mentioning where it grows and the way in which He describes its fruits. Al-Saadi: 704.\nWhat is learned from describing the tree that it grows in the bottom of the Hellfire?\nطَلۡعُهَا كَأَنَّهُۥ رُءُوسُ ٱلشَّيَٰطِينِ ٦٥\nThis is a description of how ugly and repulsive it is. It is likened to the heads of devils, even though they have never seen them, because it is a well-established idea in people's minds that devils are ugly in appearance. Ibn Kathir: 4/12.\nAllah likens its fruits to something that is unknown which is the heads of devils. Why?\nثُمَّ إِنَّ مَرۡجِعَهُمۡ لَإِلَى ٱلۡجَحِيمِ ٦٨ إِنَّهُمۡ أَلۡفَوۡاْ ءَابَآءَهُمۡ ضَآلِّينَ ٦٩\nIt is as if one asked: What brought them to this abode? Hence, Allah says: (They found their fathers astray). Al-Saadi: 704.\nWhat is the link between these two verses?\nوَلَقَدۡ ضَلَّ قَبۡلَهُمۡ أَكۡثَرُ ٱلۡأَوَّلِينَ ٧١\nAllah describes those who went astray before them as (most of the earlier people), lest some people of weak minds become deluded by the great number of polytheists and rely on it, and to know that a great number does not justify the misguidance of the misguided, nor the sin of the sinners. Therefore, when either of them is great or few in number, it must not be a trial for those of short sight and weak minds; Allah says, (Say, \"Evil and good are not equal, even if the abundance of evil may impress you\") [5:100]. Ibn Ashur: 23/128.\nAbundance and scarcity do not indicate guidance or misguidance. Explain.\nwords\nلَمَدِينُونَWill we be reckoned and recompensed\nإِن كِدتَYou almost\nلَتُردِينِRuined me\nالمُحضَرِينَOf those brought in to Hell\nطَلعُهَاIts fruits\nلَشَوبًاA mixture\nأَلفَواThey found\nيُهرَعُونَThey hastened to follow them"],[449,"§As-Saffat\ndeeds\nSeek refuge with Allah from the diseases of lusts and doubts.\nSay, \"O Lord, grant to me righteous offspring, for You are the Hearer of prayer.\"\nAid your father and respond to his command promptly.\nguid\nBe among the doers of good by being sincere in your worship to your Lord and doing good to people.\nPurify your heart from all defilement and ask Allah for a sound heart.\nForbid what is wrong wisely when you see it, even if it comes from a closer relative, like a parent and the like.\nrefl\nإِذۡ جَآءَ رَبَّهُۥ بِقَلۡبٖ سَلِيمٍ ٨٤\nA sound heart is one that is clear of shirk and doubts. Awf Al-A'rabi said: I asked Muhammad bin Sirin: What is a sound heart? He said: Sincere advice to all people for the sake of Allah. Al-Qurtubi: 18/50.\nWhat are the qualities of the sound heart, so we may attain them?\nفَمَا ظَنُّكُم بِرَبِّ ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ٨٧\nWhat do you think the Lord of the worlds will do to you, when you worship others besides Him? This was warning them of the requital for persisting in their ascription of partners to Allah. Al-Saadi: 705.\nThis verse contains exhortation and intimidation to the polytheists. Explain.\nفَرَاغَ إِلَىٰٓ ءَالِهَتِهِمۡ فَقَالَ أَلَا تَأۡكُلُونَ ٩١\nAbrahm (u) said that only to ridicule those who worshiped these idols. Ibn Juzay: 2/238.\nHow did Abraham (u) speak to the idols while they were inanimate objects?\nوَقَالَ إِنِّي ذَاهِبٌ إِلَىٰ رَبِّي سَيَهۡدِينِ ٩٩\nThis verse is a proof of migration and social isolation. Abraham (u) was the first to do that when Allah saved him from the fire, he said: (I am going to my Lord), which means: I will migrate from my home and the home of my people and my birth place to another place where I can worship my Lord. Al-Qurtubi: 18/59.\nWhen is it ordained for the believer to go into social isolation or migrate?\nرَبِّ هَبۡ لِي مِنَ ٱلصَّٰلِحِينَ ١٠٠\nThe offspring is described as righteous because the blessing of having an offspring who is righteous is ideal, for the righteousness of the offspring is a source of joy for the fathers. Moreover, their righteousness leads them to be dutiful toward their parents. Ibn Ashur: 23/148.\nExplain the importance of supplicating Allah for righteous offspring.\nفَلَمَّا بَلَغَ مَعَهُ ٱلسَّعۡيَ قَالَ يَٰبُنَيَّ إِنِّيٓ أَرَىٰ فِي ٱلۡمَنَامِ أَنِّيٓ أَذۡبَحُكَ فَٱنظُرۡ مَاذَا تَرَىٰۚ قَالَ يَٰٓأَبَتِ ٱفۡعَلۡ مَا تُؤۡمَرُۖ سَتَجِدُنِيٓ إِن شَآءَ ٱللَّهُ مِنَ ٱلصَّٰبِرِينَ ١٠٢\nIf it is said: Why did Abraham (u) consult with his son Ishmael (u) in a matter that was decreed by Allah? The answer is: He did not consult him to go along with what he would say, rather, he wanted to let him know what he intended to do so that Ishmael's heart would be firm and resolve to have patience; he replied to his father with the best answer. Ibn Juzay: 2/238.\nWhy did Abraham (u) consult with his son in a matter that was decreed by Allah?\nسَتَجِدُنِيٓ إِن شَآءَ ٱللَّهُ مِنَ ٱلصَّٰبِرِينَ ١٠٢\nIshmael told his father that he had resolved to patience, and he linked that to the will of Allah, because nothing happens except by Allah's will. Al-Saadi: 706.\nIshmael mentioned the will of Allah alongside his patience. Why?\nwords\nوَتَرَكنَا عَلَيهِWe left for him a favorable mention\nفِي الآخِرِينَAmong later generations\nشِيعَتِهِThose who followed his religion and way\nأَئِفكًا آلِهَةًIs it false gods that you seek to worship\nفَنَظَرَHe cast a look at the stars, thinking about an excuse for not going out with them\nسَقِيمٌSick; diseased, weak, or sick of your worshiping other than Allah\nيَزِفُّونَThey came hastening and anger"],[450,"§As-Saffat\ndeeds\nSmiling at your brother, helping your neighbor carry his luggage, or saying a kind word to your colleagues is all part of doing good.\nSay: “O Allah, guide me to the straight path.”\nGive out a tape or pamphlet to your collogues or around your neighborhood inviting them to Allah.\nguid\nLineage and power do not save the servant, rather, what counts is the righteousness of the deeds after the mercy of the Most Merciful.\nKnow that relief comes after hardship and distress, so, do not despair. Whoever gives up something for the sake of Allah, Allah will give him something much better instead.\nCalling upon other than Allah is contrary to piety, so, make sure to attain piety by calling upon Him alone.\nrefl\nفَلَمَّآ أَسۡلَمَا وَتَلَّهُۥ لِلۡجَبِينِ ١٠٣\nThey submitted and followed Allah's command. Ibn Abbas said: He laid him on one side of his face; the forehead is between the two sides. Al-Baghawi: 3/667.\nWhat does this expression indicate, (they both submitted)?\nقَدۡ صَدَّقۡتَ ٱلرُّءۡيَآۚ\nMeaning: The purpose of your dream has been fulfilled by your laying down your son to sacrifice him. Ibn Kathir: 4/17.\nHow did he fulfill his vision despite not sacrificing his son?\nإِنَّ هَٰذَا لَهُوَ ٱلۡبَلَٰٓؤُاْ ٱلۡمُبِينُ ١٠٦\nAbraham (u) was the close friend of the Most Gracious, and close friendship is the highest level of love; it is a level of love in which there is no room to love anything else, a level which dictates that one be attached to one's beloved with all of one’s heart. As part of Abraham’s heart became attached to his son Ishmael, Allah wanted to make his entire heart attached to Him, and to test how sincere and strong the bond of close friendship was. So, He commanded him to sacrifice the one whose love had competed with the love of his Lord. But when Abraham gave precedence to the love of Allah over his own desires, and resolved to sacrifice his son, all attachment to competitors was removed from his heart, whereupon there was no longer any benefit in sacrificing him. Al-Saadi: 706.\nHow was this incident a trial and purification of Abraham's (u) heart?\nوَفَدَيۡنَٰهُ بِذِبۡحٍ عَظِيمٖ ١٠٧\nIt was great it was the ransom for Ishmael, one of the sublime acts of worship, a means of drawing closer to Allah, and a precedent to be followed until the Day of Resurrection. Al-Saadi: 706.\nThe ransom was described as (great). Why?\nوَتَرَكۡنَا عَلَيۡهِ فِي ٱلۡأٓخِرِينَ ١٠٨ سَلَٰمٌ عَلَىٰٓ إِبۡرَٰهِيمَ ١٠٩\nAbraham (u) supplicated by saying: (And grant me an honorable mention among the later generations) [26:84], hence, Allah left for him favorable mention among later generations, while He left evil mention for Pharaoh and the likes of him. Al-Tabari: 21/91.\nWhen Allah is pleased with someone, He leaves a sign for him after his death. What is it?\nوَبَٰرَكۡنَا عَلَيۡهِ وَعَلَىٰٓ إِسۡحَٰقَۚ وَمِن ذُرِّيَّتِهِمَا مُحۡسِنٞ وَظَالِمٞ لِّنَفۡسِهِۦ مُبِينٞ ١١٣\nThis indicates that the evilness or goodness of a person is not linked to his creed or lineage. A pious person may beget a wicked son, and the opposite is true. Moreover, corrupted offspring do not diminish their fathers, because what is important is one's good morals and righteous deeds. As for the righteousness of the fathers, it compliments the good offsprings and motivates them to attain the best morals. Ibn Ashur: 23/162.\nThe wickedness or goodness of a person is not linked to his creed or lineage. Explain.\nوَبَٰرَكۡنَا عَلَيۡهِ وَعَلَىٰٓ إِسۡحَٰقَۚ وَمِن ذُرِّيَّتِهِمَا مُحۡسِنٞ وَظَالِمٞ لِّنَفۡسِهِۦ مُبِينٞ ١١٣\nWhen Allah mentions the blessing and abundance of the offspring, He says that some did good and some did evil, and those who did evil would not be availed by the fact that their forefathers were Prophets. Even though the Jews descend from Isaac and the Arabs descend from Ishmael, the fact remains that good and evil, believers and disbelievers are all not the same. Al-Qurtubi: 18/83.\nWill the righteousness of your father be suffice you? Will his wickedness harm you?\nwords\nأَسلَمَاThey submitted to Allah's command\nوَتَلَّهُ لِلجَبِينِHe laid him on his forehead\nوَفَدَينَاهُWe ransomed him\nبِذِبحٍWith a sacrifice , a ram\nأَتَدعُونَ بَعلًاDo you worship an idol called Ba'l"],[451,"§As-Saffat\ndeeds\nSay, \"O Allah, make me among your chosen servants.\"\nRemember one of your acquaintances whom you tried inviting to the right path until you despaired of his guidance, then ask for Allah's forgiveness for your despair, as it is a sin against Allah, the Almighty.\nExalt Allah, so that He may protect you from affliction.\nguid\nReflect on the dire warning to those who denied and maligned the Messengers .\nKnow that the right mind leads the believing servant to take heed and reflect on the ways of Allah, the Almighty.\nKnow that one of the worst fabrications is that which is about Allah, the Almighty.\nrefl\nسَلَٰمٌ عَلَىٰٓ إِلۡ يَاسِينَ إِنَّا ١٣٠ كَذَٰلِكَ نَجۡزِي ٱلۡمُحۡسِنِينَ ١٣١ إِنَّهُۥ مِنۡ عِبَادِنَا ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ ١٣٢\nElias' story indicates that the Messenger's duty is to convey the message, and it is not essential for him to witness the destruction of those who reject him; this responds to the polytheists who said: (When will this warning come to pass, if you are truthful) [10:48]. Allah says, (Say, “My Lord, if You show me what they are warned of ` My Lord, then do not place me among the wrongdoing people ` We are surely able to show you what We have warned them) [23:93-95]. Ibn Ashur: 23/170.\nThe preacher should convey his message and should not wait for the punishment of those who did not accept it. Given this verse, explain this concept.\nوَإِنَّكُمۡ لَتَمُرُّونَ عَلَيۡهِم مُّصۡبِحِينَ ١٣٧ وَبِٱلَّيۡلِۚ أَفَلَا تَعۡقِلُونَ ١٣٨\nMeaning: You pass by their ruins during the daytime and night when you travel back and forth (Then will you not use reason) so you be admonished by their fate. Al-Baghawi: 3/678.\nThe ruins of former people is for admonishment and warning, not for entertainment and pastime. Explain in light of this verse.\nوَإِنَّ يُونُسَ لَمِنَ ٱلۡمُرۡسَلِينَ ١٣٩ إِذۡ أَبَقَ إِلَى ٱلۡفُلۡكِ ٱلۡمَشۡحُونِ ١٤٠ فَسَاهَمَ فَكَانَ مِنَ ٱلۡمُدۡحَضِينَ ١٤١ فَٱلۡتَقَمَهُ ٱلۡحُوتُ وَهُوَ مُلِيمٞ ١٤٢ فَلَوۡلَآ أَنَّهُۥ كَانَ مِنَ ٱلۡمُسَبِّحِينَ ١٤٣ لَلَبِثَ فِي بَطۡنِهِۦٓ إِلَىٰ يَوۡمِ يُبۡعَثُونَ ١٤٤\nKnow that the aim of mentioning Jonah here was to console the Prophet (ﷺ) for carrying the load of the Message by informing him that it was a heavy load for the Messengers before him too. Hence, the Prophet's (ﷺ) high rank became apparent for his patience and uncomplaining. Moreover, it was to inform all the people that he was commanded by Allah to persist in calling them to the true religion because the polytheists used to blame him for his persistence in calling them during different times and situations. Ibn Ashur: 23/178.\nWhat is the aim of mentioning the story of Jonah (u)?\nوَإِنَّ يُونُسَ لَمِنَ ٱلۡمُرۡسَلِينَ ١٣٩ إِذۡ أَبَقَ إِلَى ٱلۡفُلۡكِ ٱلۡمَشۡحُونِ ١٤٠\nAllah does not mention the cause of his anger or the sin that he committed, because there is no benefit for us in mentioning that. Rather, what benefits us is to tell us that he committed a sin and Allah punished him for it, despite the fact that he was one of the noble Messengers, then He saved him after that, and absolved him of blame, and made available to him the means of well-being. Al-Saadi: 707.\nWhat do you learn from knowing that one of the Prophets was punished for his sin?\nإِذۡ أَبَقَ إِلَى ٱلۡفُلۡكِ ٱلۡمَشۡحُونِ ١٤٠\nMeaning: He wanted to escape so he took to the sea. In the Arabic text, the word \"abaqa\" means the flight and escape of a slave from his master without permission. It is used here for Jonah since he is a slave of Allah, and so that is the meaning of \"Ibaq\" in Arabic. Ibn Atiyah: 4/485.\n\"Ibaq\" is used to describe the flight of a slave from his master, so why is it used here to describe Jonah who was a free man?\nإِذۡ أَبَقَ إِلَى ٱلۡفُلۡكِ ٱلۡمَشۡحُونِ ١٤٠\nMeaning: He escaped to the ship that was full of people, and the reason for his escape was his anger at his people since they did not believe him. Ibn Juzay: 2/241.\nWhy did Allah's Prophet Jonah (u) escape to the fully loaded ship?\nفَلَوۡلَآ أَنَّهُۥ كَانَ مِنَ ٱلۡمُسَبِّحِينَ ١٤٣\nAllah mentions that Jonah was one of those who exalt Allah, and that his exaltation of Allah was the cause for his deliverance, hence, it is said that a righteous deed lifts its doer when he stumbles. Alhasan said: Jonah did not perform prayer inside the whale's belly, but he had done good deeds during times of prosperity, hence, Allah remembered him during the time of adversity. Al-Qurtubi: 18/99.\nWhat was the cause for Jonah's (u) deliverance?\nwords\nالغَابِرِينَThose who remained behind in punishment\nأَبَقَHe fled his city without his Lord's leave\nفَسَاهَمَThe ship's passengers cast lots to reduce its weight to save it from drowning\nالمُدحَضِينَThose who lost the lots\nفَالتَقَمَهُIt swallowed him\nمُلِيمٌA blameworthy\nفَنَبَذنَاهُWe cast him out of the whale's belly"],[452,"§As-Saffat\ndeeds\nSay, \"Exalted is Allah and praise is to Him, by the multitude of His creation, by His Pleasure, by the weight of His Throne, and by the ink (extent) of His Words.\"\nStand straight in line to perform prayer.\nShare a message of support to the Muslim Ummah, so you will be among Allah’s servants who stand up for his religion.\nguid\nBe certain that Allah's religion will inevitably be victorious.\nAllah, the Almighty, commands us to turn away from the deniers.\nExalt and glorify Allah when you hear the words of liars.\nrefl\nوَجَعَلُواْ بَيۡنَهُۥ وَبَيۡنَ ٱلۡجِنَّةِ نَسَبٗاۚ وَلَقَدۡ عَلِمَتِ ٱلۡجِنَّةُ إِنَّهُمۡ لَمُحۡضَرُونَ ١٥٨\nMeaning: These polytheists claimed that there was a kinship between Allah and the jinn. But the jinn knew that they would be brought before Allah so that He would requite them as humiliated slaves. If there was any kinship between them and Him, they would not be like that. Al-Saadi: 708.\nWhat is the aim of stating that the jinn will be brought for reckoning?\nفَإِنَّكُمۡ وَمَا تَعۡبُدُونَ ١٦١ مَآ أَنتُمۡ عَلَيۡهِ بِفَٰتِنِينَ ١٦٢ إِلَّا مَنۡ هُوَ صَالِ ٱلۡجَحِيمِ ١٦٣\nThese verses indicate that devils cannot misguide anyone except whom Allah decreed His misguidance, but if Allah knew that he would be guided, He would have placed prevention between him and them. Al-Qurtubi: 18/112.\nCan satan misguide you whenever he wants? What do you learn from that?\nوَمَا مِنَّآ إِلَّا لَهُۥ مَقَامٞ مَّعۡلُومٞ ١٦٤\nMeaning: Each one of us has a designated position in the heavens in which he worship Allah. Ibn Abbas said: There is not a span in the heavens except at which an angel is praying or glorifying Allah. Al-Baghawi: 3/681.\nDescribe the angels’ state in their worship.\nوَإِنَّا لَنَحۡنُ ٱلصَّآفُّونَ ١٦٥\nMeaning: Those who stand lined up in rows for worship, and that is why Muslims are enjoined to straighten their rows for prayer to be like the angels. No other followers of any religion pray in rows except Muslims. Ibn Juzay: 2/244.\nThe angels are the most powerful among all creatures, yet they are most humble before Allah. Explain in light of this verse.\nوَإِنَّا لَنَحۡنُ ٱلصَّآفُّونَ ١٦٥ وَإِنَّا لَنَحۡنُ ٱلۡمُسَبِّحُونَ ١٦٦\nAbu Nadhrah said: When Iqamah (starting time) of prayer was called, Omar used to face the people and say: O people, straighten your rows, as Allah wants for you the guidance of the angels, (and we are indeed those who stand lined up in rows ` And indeed, we are those who exalt Allah); straighten your rows; you, so and so, come forward, you, so and so, go back. After straightening the rows, he would go forward to lead them in prayer. Al-Tabari: 21/128.\nThe believers follow the example of the angels in an act of veneration of Allah. Explain.\nسُبۡحَٰنَ رَبِّكَ رَبِّ ٱلۡعِزَّةِ عَمَّا يَصِفُونَ ١٨٠\nHaving mentioned in this Surah many of the vile things that they said and attributed to Him, Allah now declares Himself to be far above all that, as He says: (Exalted is your Lord). Al-Saadi: 709.\nAllah ends this Surah with the exaltation of Himself. Why?\nوَٱلۡحَمۡدُ لِلَّهِ رَبِّ ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ١٨٢\n(And all praise be to Allah, the Lord of the worlds): Allah says, All praise be to Allah, the Lord of the prominent beings, jinn and mankind, with all sincerity to Him and no one else, for every blessing upon His servants is from Him. Therefore, all praise be solely to Him without partners just as all blessings upon them come solely from Him without partners. Al-Tabari: 21/134.\nAll praise must be solely to Allah, the Most High, for all the blessings. Why?\nwords\nمَا لَكُم كَيفَ تَحكُمُونَHow wretched is your judgment\nسُلطَانٌProof\nلَمُحضَرُونَThe disbelievers will be brought to punishment on the Day of Resurrection\nبِفَاتِنِينَYou misguide others\nصَالِ الجَحِيمِHe who will enter and burn in the Hellfire\nالصَّآفُّونَThose who stand lined up in rows\nبِسَاحَتِهِمOn their courtyard"],[453,"§Sad\ndeeds\nSay, \"None is worthy of worship but Allah alone, Who has no partner. To Him belongs all sovereignty and all praise, and He is Capable over all things.\"\nSay: \"O Allah, defeat the disbelievers who avert others from your path and are hostile to the people of your religion.\"\nRead a book on interpretation that explains the portion you memorize from the Quran.\nguid\nTake heed of what happened to former generations that were destroyed by Allah.\nOne of the ways of Allah that will remain until the end of time is that the preachers of truth will be subjected to insults and mocking , but that will not harm you.\nDo not be envious of the blessings of people, for by doing so you are objecting to Allah’s judgment and decree.\nrefl\nوَٱلۡقُرۡءَانِ ذِي ٱلذِّكۡرِ ١ بَلِ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ فِي عِزَّةٖ وَشِقَاقٖ ٢\nMeaning: In this Quran, there is a reminder for those who will be reminded and a lesson for those who will learn a lesson, but the disbelievers will not benefit from it because they (are in pride), which means arrogance and tribalism. (And dissension), they are stubbornly opposed to it and go against it. Ibn Kathir: 4/27.\nIn light of this verse, list the things that prevent one from benefitting from the Quran.\nبَلِ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ فِي عِزَّةٖ وَشِقَاقٖ ٢\nThe Arabic word used for dissension is \"shiqaq\", and some scholars said: \"Shiqaq\" root comes from hardship, which indicates that the stubborn dissenter strives to cause hardship to whoever stubbornly opposes him. Some other scholars said: \"Shiqaq\" comes from splitting a stick, which refers to dispute and division. Al-Shanqiti: 6/330.\nThe disbelievers are described as, in (dissention). Why?\nوَعَجِبُوٓاْ أَن جَآءَهُم مُّنذِرٞ مِّنۡهُمۡۖ وَقَالَ ٱلۡكَٰفِرُونَ هَٰذَا سَٰحِرٞ كَذَّابٌ ٤\nThe demonstrative pronoun, (this), which they used to refer to the Prophet (ﷺ) was intended to belittle the likes of him. Ibn Ashur: 23/209.\nThe polytheists used the demonstrative pronoun, (this) to refer to the Prophet (ﷺ). Why?\nوَٱنطَلَقَ ٱلۡمَلَأُ مِنۡهُمۡ أَنِ ٱمۡشُواْ وَٱصۡبِرُواْ عَلَىٰٓ ءَالِهَتِكُمۡۖ إِنَّ هَٰذَا لَشَيۡءٞ يُرَادُ ٦\n(Indeed, this is a thing intended), it is deliberate, and he has an ulterior motive and bad intentions. This was a specious argument that could only be accepted by foolish people, for when a person calls others to something, whether it is true or not, his view is not to be rejected by casting aspersions on his intentions, because his intentions and deeds will affect him only. Rather, it is to be refuted by presenting something to counter his arguments and invalidates them through proof and evidence. Al-Saadi: 710.\nGiven this verse, explain how you would respond to those who cast doubts about the intentions of the scholars and preachers.\nأَءُنزِلَ عَلَيۡهِ ٱلذِّكۡرُ مِنۢ بَيۡنِنَاۚ بَلۡ هُمۡ فِي شَكّٖ مِّن ذِكۡرِيۚ بَل لَّمَّا يَذُوقُواْ عَذَابِ ٨\nMeaning: They were deluded by My respite; had they tasted My punishment, all of their doubts would have been gone. Al-Qurtubi: 18/135-136.\nWhat is the reason for the disbelievers’ delusion and persistence on shirk?\nجُندٞ مَّا هُنَالِكَ مَهۡزُومٞ مِّنَ ٱلۡأَحۡزَابِ ١١\nThis was a warning to them of their defeat in battle, and it came to pass in the battle of Badr and others. Ibn Juzay: 2/248.\nAllah promised His Prophet the defeat of the polytheists at the beginning of his mission in Makkah while the Muslims were oppressed. When did this promise come to pass?\nكَذَّبَتۡ قَبۡلَهُمۡ قَوۡمُ نُوحٖ وَعَادٞ وَفِرۡعَوۡنُ ذُو ٱلۡأَوۡتَادِ ١٢\nPharaoh is described as (the owner of stakes) because of his great kingdom and power, but all of that could not ward off Allah's punishment. Ibn Ashur: 23/220.\nPharaoh is described as (the owner of stakes). Why?\nwords\nالمِلَّةِ الآخِرَةِThe religion of our fathers and Christianity\nاختلاقA fabrication\nفَليَرتَقُوا فِي الأَسبَابِlet them ascend to the heaven and prevent the revelation\nوَأَصحَابُ الأَيكَةِThe dwellers of the trees and gardens; people of Shu'ayb (u)\nفَوَاقٍReturn\nقِطَّنَاOur share of punishment"],[454,"§Sad\ndeeds\nSet for yourself a time to glorify and remember Allah in the morning and evening.\nSay: \"O Allah, I seek refuge in You from going astray or being led astray, from slipping or being caused to slip, from wronging others or being wronged, and from behaving or being treated ignorantly.\"\nAsk for Allah's forgiveness a hundred times, then ask Him to accept it.\nguid\nRecall and talk often about the stories of the Prophets and the righteous.\nBear with patience the annoyance caused by others.\nBeware of following your whim, for it is the cause of misguidance to you and others, and uphold justice and truth in your judgment.\nrefl\nٱصۡبِرۡ عَلَىٰ مَا يَقُولُونَ وَٱذۡكُرۡ عَبۡدَنَا دَاوُۥدَ ذَا ٱلۡأَيۡدِۖ إِنَّهُۥٓ أَوَّابٌ ١٧\nThe mention of David and other Prophets who came after him in this Surah is to console the Prophet (ﷺ), to promise him of victory, to relieve his hardship, and to help him attain the level of patience of which he is enjoined. When Allah mentions His blessings upon David, such as the subjection of birds and mountains, strengthening of his kingdom, giving him wisdom and discernment in speech, then, nearness to Allah and a good place of return in the Hereafter – it is like saying: O Muhammad, as We blessed David with all these blessings, We will bless you, so bear with patience and do not let their words grieve you. Ibn Juzay: 2/249.\nWhat is the link between Allah's command to Prophet Muhammad (ﷺ) to be patient and to mention David?\nٱصۡبِرۡ عَلَىٰ مَا يَقُولُونَ وَٱذۡكُرۡ عَبۡدَنَا دَاوُۥدَ ذَا ٱلۡأَيۡدِۖ إِنَّهُۥٓ أَوَّابٌ ١٧\nOne of the lessons learned from the story of David is that Allah praises and loves a person to have energy when doing acts of obedience and worship, and to be strong in both physical and mental terms because if a person is strong, it will result in performing more acts of obedience properly, which cannot be done when a person is weak and has no resolve. The individual should seek means of developing strength and energy, and not become lazy and slow, as that will lead to loss of energy that will weaken one's resolve. Al-Saadi: 713.\nAllah likes the servant's strength in His obedience. Explain that, given His description of David (u) as (the man of strength).\nوَءَاتَيۡنَٰهُ ٱلۡحِكۡمَةَ وَفَصۡلَ ٱلۡخِطَابِ ٢٠\nAnother lesson from the story of David is that one of the greatest blessings that Allah can bestow upon His servant is to bless him with beneficial knowledge so that he knows how to judge between people, as Allah blessed His servant David (u) with such knowledge. Al-Saadi: 713.\nWhat do we learn from Allah's blessing of wisdom upon David?\nإِنَّ هَٰذَآ أَخِي لَهُۥ تِسۡعٞ وَتِسۡعُونَ نَعۡجَةٗ وَلِيَ نَعۡجَةٞ وَٰحِدَةٞ فَقَالَ أَكۡفِلۡنِيهَا وَعَزَّنِي فِي ٱلۡخِطَابِ ٢٣ قَالَ لَقَدۡ ظَلَمَكَ بِسُؤَالِ نَعۡجَتِكَ إِلَىٰ نِعَاجِهِۦۖ وَإِنَّ كَثِيرٗا مِّنَ ٱلۡخُلَطَآءِ لَيَبۡغِي بَعۡضُهُمۡ عَلَىٰ بَعۡضٍ إِلَّا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ وَعَمِلُواْ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ وَقَلِيلٞ مَّا هُمۡۗ وَظَنَّ دَاوُۥدُ أَنَّمَا فَتَنَّٰهُ فَٱسۡتَغۡفَرَ رَبَّهُۥ وَخَرَّۤ رَاكِعٗاۤ وَأَنَابَ۩ ٢٤\nIn the books of the Children of Israel, some parts of the story of David are narrated inappropriately, and some earlier Muslim storytellers used to repeat that, so Ali bin Abi Talib (t) said: Whoever narrates what these storytellers are saying about David (u), I will punish him for slandering twice for his transgression against the one whom Allah has raised high. Ibn Atiyah: 4/499.\nWhat is mentioned about Ali bin Abi Talib (t) regarding David’s story preserves the status of Prophethood. Explain.\nوَإِنَّ كَثِيرٗا مِّنَ ٱلۡخُلَطَآءِ لَيَبۡغِي بَعۡضُهُمۡ عَلَىٰ بَعۡضٍ إِلَّا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ وَعَمِلُواْ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ وَقَلِيلٞ مَّا هُمۡۗ وَظَنَّ دَاوُۥدُ أَنَّمَا فَتَنَّٰهُ فَٱسۡتَغۡفَرَ رَبَّهُۥ وَخَرَّۤ رَاكِعٗاۤ وَأَنَابَ۩ ٢٤\n(Except those who believe and do righteous deeds), because they do not oppress anyone. (And how few they are), those who are righteous. Al-Qurtubi: 18/172.\nThis verse emphasizes the importance of considering belief and righteousness when selecting a partner. Explain ?\nوَظَنَّ دَاوُۥدُ أَنَّمَا فَتَنَّٰهُ فَٱسۡتَغۡفَرَ رَبَّهُۥ وَخَرَّۤ رَاكِعٗاۤ وَأَنَابَ۩ ٢٤ فَغَفَرۡنَا لَهُۥ ذَٰلِكَۖ\nSeeking forgiveness and doing acts of worship, especially prayer, are among the means of absolving sins, because Allah linked the forgiveness of David’s sin to his prayer for forgiveness and his prostration. Al-Saadi: 713.\nGiven this verse, how important is performing prayer as a means of absolving sins?\nيَٰدَاوُۥدُ إِنَّا جَعَلۡنَٰكَ خَلِيفَةٗ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ فَٱحۡكُم بَيۡنَ ٱلنَّاسِ بِٱلۡحَقِّ وَلَا تَتَّبِعِ ٱلۡهَوَىٰ فَيُضِلَّكَ عَن سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِۚ إِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ يَضِلُّونَ عَن سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ لَهُمۡ عَذَابٞ شَدِيدُۢ بِمَا نَسُواْ يَوۡمَ ٱلۡحِسَابِ ٢٦\nMost levels of perfections are hard for the soul because they reform and lift it high and above the level of animalistic inclinations, as the indulgence in following these inclinations will inevitably lead to falling in lowness. Ibn Ashur: 23/244.\nFollowing one's whims contravenes reaching perfection. Explain in light of this verse.\nwords\nذَا الأَيدِThe man of strength in worship and in war\nأَوَّابٌHe was constantly turned to Allah\nوَلاَ تُشطِطDo not be unjust\nأَكفِلنِيهَاHand it over to me\nالخُلَطَاءِPartners\nلَزُلفَىA place of nearness\nمَآبٍA place of return"],[455,"§Sad\ndeeds\nRead a surah from the last chapter of the Quran and its interpretation, then reflect on its lessons, knowledge, and practical requirements.\nThink of something you own that distracts you from worship and donate it for the sake of Allah, so that He may reward you with something much better.\nFollowing the example of the Prophets, ask Allah, the Almighty, to give you the best of this world and the Hereafter.\nguid\nBe aware that people of sound minds are those who benefit and reflect on admonishments.\nBeware of becoming preoccupied with a worldly matter that distracts you from the obedience of Allah, the Almighty.\nConstantly return to Allah in repentance whenever you are in distress or afflicted, or had committed a sin.\nrefl\nكِتَٰبٌ أَنزَلۡنَٰهُ إِلَيۡكَ مُبَٰرَكٞ لِّيَدَّبَّرُوٓاْ ءَايَٰتِهِۦ وَلِيَتَذَكَّرَ أُوْلُواْ ٱلۡأَلۡبَٰبِ ٢٩\nThe obvious meaning of this verse indicates that reflection is one of the aims of sending down the Quran. Therefore, the recital of the Quran is better than reading quickly through it, as reflection can only be attained with reciting. Ibn Atiyah: 4/503.\nClarify the link between the reflection on the Quran and its recital.\nكِتَٰبٌ أَنزَلۡنَٰهُ إِلَيۡكَ مُبَٰرَكٞ لِّيَدَّبَّرُوٓاْ ءَايَٰتِهِۦ وَلِيَتَذَكَّرَ أُوْلُواْ ٱلۡأَلۡبَٰبِ ٢٩\nAll the verses in the Quran are blessed since they are either guiding to something good, or averting from evil and corruption, and that brings about what is good in the present and the future, and there is no blessing greater than that. Ibn Ashur: 23/251.\nAll the verses in the Book of Allah are blessed. Explain in light of this verse.\nكِتَٰبٌ أَنزَلۡنَٰهُ إِلَيۡكَ مُبَٰرَكٞ لِّيَدَّبَّرُوٓاْ ءَايَٰتِهِۦ وَلِيَتَذَكَّرَ أُوْلُواْ ٱلۡأَلۡبَٰبِ ٢٩\n(People of understanding), are those of sound minds. This is an allusion to those who were not reminded by the Quran that they were not of those who have sound minds. Moreover, those who are reminded are the Muslims who listen to speech and follow the best of it. They are the ones who reflected on its verses and deduced meanings of which they were not aware, while the disbelievers turned away from reflecting on it, and hence, missed being reminded by it. Ibn Ashur: 23/253.\nIn light of this verse, what is the sign of the people of understanding?\nفَقَالَ إِنِّيٓ أَحۡبَبۡتُ حُبَّ ٱلۡخَيۡرِ عَن ذِكۡرِ رَبِّي حَتَّىٰ تَوَارَتۡ بِٱلۡحِجَابِ ٣٢\nThe horses are called (good things) because goodness is tied to the foreheads of horses, as they bring about either a reward in the Hereafter or war booty in this world. Al-Baghawi: 3/703.\nThe horses are called (good things). Why?\nقَالَ رَبِّ ٱغۡفِرۡ لِي وَهَبۡ لِي مُلۡكٗا لَّا يَنۢبَغِي لِأَحَدٖ مِّنۢ بَعۡدِيٓۖ إِنَّكَ أَنتَ ٱلۡوَهَّابُ ٣٥\nHe asked for forgiveness before requesting a kingdom, because religious matters were more important to them than worldly ones. Ibn Juzay: 2/255\nSolomon (u) asked for forgiveness before requesting a kingdom. Why?\nقَالَ رَبِّ ٱغۡفِرۡ لِي وَهَبۡ لِي مُلۡكٗا لَّا يَنۢبَغِي لِأَحَدٖ مِّنۢ بَعۡدِيٓۖ إِنَّكَ أَنتَ ٱلۡوَهَّابُ ٣٥ فَسَخَّرۡنَا لَهُ ٱلرِّيحَ تَجۡرِي بِأَمۡرِهِۦ رُخَآءً حَيۡثُ أَصَابَ ٣٦\nAlhasan said that when the horses were brought to Prophet Solomon (u), he became so absorbed in reviewing them, that he forgot to offer his Asr Prayer (until it disappeared into the veil of darkness), so he became angry for the sake of Allah, and ordered the horses to be slaughtered. Then, Allah replaced them with something faster for him, the wind blowing gently by His command to wherever he wished. Al-Tabari: 21/201-202.\nGiven this verse, explain that whoever gives up something for the sake of Allah, Allah will give him something much better instead.\nوَٱذۡكُرۡ عَبۡدَنَآ أَيُّوبَ إِذۡ نَادَىٰ رَبَّهُۥٓ أَنِّي مَسَّنِيَ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنُ بِنُصۡبٖ وَعَذَابٍ ٤١\nAllah mentions this particular situation of Prophet Job when he called to his Lord because it manifested his reliance upon Allah and Allah's answer to his call by removing his hardship. Ibn Ashur: 23/268.\nAllah mentions this particular situation of Prophet Job (u) when he called to his Lord. Why?\nwords\nالصَّافِنَاتُHorses standing on three legs and raises the fourth due to its beauty and ability\nالجِيَادُWell-bred and fast horses\nفَطَفِقَHe began\nمَسحًا بِالسُّوقِ وَالأَعنَاقِHe began passing his hand over their legs and necks, or striking them with the sword for the sake of Allah\nرُخَاءًGently at his command\nبِنُصبٍHardship"],[456,"§Sad\ndeeds\nRecall a situation in which you were patient, and ask Allah to record your patience in your good deeds.\nRemember an oath you took and try to fulfill it, in reverence of Allah's command.\nAsk Allah not to let worldly affairs be your principal concern.\nguid\nAllah may afflict those whom He loves among His servants in order to increase their status and elevate their ranks.\nA relationship that is built on the displeasure of Allah will turn into enmity in the Hereafter.\nDo not be a cause for anyone to sin.\nrefl\nوَخُذۡ بِيَدِكَ ضِغۡثٗا فَٱضۡرِب بِّهِۦ وَلَا تَحۡنَثۡۗ إِنَّا وَجَدۡنَٰهُ صَابِرٗاۚ\nProphet Job (u) became angry with his wife, so he swore an oath that if Allah healed him, he would lash her a hundred times. After Allah healed him, how could her service, mercy, compassion, and kindness be repaid with a beating? So, Allah showed him a way out, which was to take a bundle of thin grass, with one hundred stems, and hit her with it once. Thus, he fulfilled his oath and avoided breaking his vow. This was the solution and way out for one who had fear of Allah and turned to Him in repentance. Ibn Kathir: 4/41.\nWhen one has true fear of Allah, Allah will make a way out for him. Explain, given this verse\nوَٱذۡكُرۡ عِبَٰدَنَآ إِبۡرَٰهِيمَ وَإِسۡحَٰقَ وَيَعۡقُوبَ أُوْلِي ٱلۡأَيۡدِي وَٱلۡأَبۡصَٰرِ ٤٥\nTheir strength was in doing righteous deeds. In the Arabic text, the word used for strength is \"hands\", because deeds are mostly done using the hands. They had insights and knowledge. In the Arabic text, the word used for insights is \"sights\", which means insights, similar to describing someone who has insight by saying: He can see things. Ibn Juzay: 2/257.\nAllah praises His Prophets, saying, (men of strength and insight). Explain.\nهَٰذَا ذِكۡرٞۚ وَإِنَّ لِلۡمُتَّقِينَ لَحُسۡنَ مَـَٔابٖ ٤٩\n(This is a reminder), an excellent mention and a lasting honor for them in this world. (And the righteous will surely have a good place of return), in addition to the excellent mention in this world, they will have a good place of return in the Hereafter. Al-Qurtubi: 18/226.\nThis verse contains some of the rewards for the righteous in this world and the Hereafter. Explain\nمُّفَتَّحَةٗ لَّهُمُ ٱلۡأَبۡوَٰبُ ٥٠\nThis is also indicative of perfect security, for in the gardens of perpetual abode there is nothing that would require closing and locking of gates (or doors). Al-Saadi: 715.\nThis verse indicates a great blessing bestowed by Allah upon the believers. What is it?\n۞وَعِندَهُمۡ قَٰصِرَٰتُ ٱلطَّرۡفِ أَتۡرَابٌ ٥٢\n(And they will have) will be their wives of wide, beautiful eyes (of modest gaze) and look only at their husbands, and their husbands will look only at them, because of the beauty that all will possess, and the love that each will have for the other; they will have no desire for any other companion and will not think of any replacement. Al-Saadi: 715.\nDescribing the maidens in Paradise as (of modest gaze) is indicative of a quality that a Muslim woman should have so it may be a reason for her to enter Paradise. What is it?\nإِنَّ هَٰذَا لَرِزۡقُنَا مَا لَهُۥ مِن نَّفَادٍ ٥٤\nWhenever the dwellers of Paradise pick a fruit and eat it, another one will appear in its place, and this will continue for eternity. Al-Tabari: 21/223.\nThis verse reveals the difference between the fruits of Paradise and that of this world. Explain.\nقَالُواْ بَلۡ أَنتُمۡ لَا مَرۡحَبَۢا بِكُمۡۖ أَنتُمۡ قَدَّمۡتُمُوهُ لَنَاۖ فَبِئۡسَ ٱلۡقَرَارُ ٦٠\nMeaning: You called us to disobedience, and that is a terrible place for both of us. The followers will say, Our Lord, whoever brought this on us, give him double punishment in the Fire. Al-Qurtubi: 18/233.\nWhat will be the condition of the followers with their disobedient leaders on the Day of Resurrection? What lesson is learned from that?\nwords\nضِغثًاA bunch of grass\nوَلاَ تَحنَثDo not break your oath to strike your wife\nأَخلَصنَاهُم بِخَالِصَةٍWe chose them for an exclusive quality\nقَاصِرَاتُ الطَّرفِThey do not look at other than their husbands\nأَترَابٌThey are of equal age\nنَفَادٍDepletion\nلَشَرَّ مَآبٍThe worst return"],[457,"§Sad\ndeeds\nAsk forgiveness from a Muslim you once ridiculed, give charity on his behalf, pray to Allah to forgive him, and repent sincerely.\nAsk refuge with Allah from the temptations of satan and from following his steps.\nAsk Allah to make you among His chosen servants.\nguid\nThe dispute among the people of Fire will be a psychological punishment on top of the physical one.\nHelp heal sicknesses of the soul such as arrogance and envy by praying for those who suffer from them.\nBeware of misplaced pride and arrogance, which is the sin for which satan entered Hell.\nrefl\nوَقَالُواْ مَا لَنَا لَا نَرَىٰ رِجَالٗا كُنَّا نَعُدُّهُم مِّنَ ٱلۡأَشۡرَارِ ٦٢\nMeaning: We thought of them as miserable who lost the pleasure of life by following Islam and settling for a harsh life. Ibn Ashur: 23/292.\nA part of their psychological punishment will be realizing their misjudgment about people in worldly life. Explain in light of this verse.\nقُلۡ إِنَّمَآ أَنَا۠ مُنذِرٞۖ وَمَا مِنۡ إِلَٰهٍ إِلَّا ٱللَّهُ ٱلۡوَٰحِدُ ٱلۡقَهَّارُ ٦٥\nThis is an affirmation of His divinity, based on definitive proof, namely His Oneness and His subjugation of all things. Subjugation is indicative of Oneness because there cannot be two subjugators who are equal in their subjugation. The One Who subjugates all things is the One Who has no equal, and He is the One Who alone deserves to be worshiped, just as He alone is the Subjugator. Al-Saadi: 716.\nAllah combines these two attributes (the One, the Prevailing). Why?\nقُلۡ هُوَ نَبَؤٌاْ عَظِيمٌ ٦٧\n(Say) to them, to alert and warn, and to motivate them: (It is great news) that is, what I am telling you about the resurrection and requital of deeds is a message of great importance; a great deal of attention must be paid to it, and it should not be overlooked. Al-Saadi: 716.\nWhen knowing that the Day of Resurrection and reckoning is great news. What should you do?\nإِلَّآ إِبۡلِيسَ ٱسۡتَكۡبَرَ وَكَانَ مِنَ ٱلۡكَٰفِرِينَ ٧٤\nA hidden trait in Iblees has surfaced, which is arrogance and disobedience, and it was not visible before that, because the angels with whom he was were the perfect company, hence, it did not stir any hidden traits in him such as arrogance and disobedience. When a newcomer joined the angels, and they were ordered to dignify him, it triggered the hidden arrogance in Iblees' soul, which led to his disbelief and disobedience. Ibn Ashur: 23/301.\nWhat was the reason for the emergence of the arrogance of Iblees?\nقَالَ يَٰٓإِبۡلِيسُ مَا مَنَعَكَ أَن تَسۡجُدَ لِمَا خَلَقۡتُ بِيَدَيَّۖ أَسۡتَكۡبَرۡتَ أَمۡ كُنتَ مِنَ ٱلۡعَالِينَ ٧٥ قَالَ أَنَا۠ خَيۡرٞ مِّنۡهُ خَلَقۡتَنِي مِن نَّارٖ وَخَلَقۡتَهُۥ مِن طِينٖ ٧٦\nThis was a rebuke from Allah to the polytheists who denied Muhammad (ﷺ) because they did follow him due to their arrogance when they said: (Has the message been revealed to him out of all of us?)[38:8], and (Is this but a human being just like yourselves?) [21:3]. So, Allah relates to them the story of Iblees and his ruin by his arrogance and claim that he was better than Adam (u). Al-Tabari: 21/239.\nWhat is the link between Iblees’ story and Quraish disbelievers’ position of our Prophet Muhammad (ﷺ)?\nقَالَ رَبِّ فَأَنظِرۡنِيٓ إِلَىٰ يَوۡمِ يُبۡعَثُونَ ٧٩ قَالَ فَإِنَّكَ مِنَ ٱلۡمُنظَرِينَ ٨٠ إِلَىٰ يَوۡمِ ٱلۡوَقۡتِ ٱلۡمَعۡلُومِ ٨١\nIblees asked Allah to give him a reprieve until the Day of Resurrection, so the Forbearing One, Who does not hasten to punish those who disobey Him, gave him a reprieve. When he knew that he was safe from destruction until the Day of Resurrection, he rebelled and transgressed and he said: (I will surely mislead them all ` Except for Your chosen servants among them). Ibn Kathir: 4/45.\nWhat is the divine attribute by which Allah gave respite to Iblees?\nقَالَ فَبِعِزَّتِكَ لَأُغۡوِيَنَّهُمۡ أَجۡمَعِينَ ٨٢\nWhen Iblees was expelled because of Adam, he swore by the might of Allah that he would misguide the children of Adam by making desires appealing to them and casting doubts about their beliefs. Al-Qurtubi: 18/240.\nWhat are Iblees' ways of misguiding the children of Adam?\nwords\nأَتَّخَذنَاهُم سِخرِيًّاIs it a mistake that we took them in ridicule\nزَاغَتOur eyes fail to see them\nبِالمَلَأِ الأَعلَىThe angels\nيَختَصِمُونَArguing over the creation of Adam (u)\nسَوَّيتُهُI completed his creation\nسَاجِدِينَA prostrate of greeting, not worshiping\nلَأُغوِيَنَّهُمI will misguide them"],[458,"§Sad, Az-Zumar\ndeeds\nSeek refuge with Allah from the Fire, for it is the fate of Iblees’ followers.\nPray to Allah that your Tawhīd (Oneness of Allah) is solely devoted to Him and not tainted by shirk or show off.\nReflect on the orbiting of the sun and moon and their useful lessons.\nguid\nIf you can ask for no reward for your calling to Allah except from Him, then do it.\nAllah, the Almighty, accepts only sincere worship, so, ensure sincerity to Him in all your deeds.\nLying about Allah, the Prophet, and the believers is condemned.\nrefl\nقُلۡ مَآ أَسۡـَٔلُكُمۡ عَلَيۡهِ مِنۡ أَجۡرٖ وَمَآ أَنَا۠ مِنَ ٱلۡمُتَكَلِّفِينَ ٨٦\nMasrouq said: We visited Abdullah bin Masoud (t) and he said to us: O people, he who has knowledge of any matter may convey it to others, but he who has no knowledge, thereof, should say: \"Allah knows best.\" It is a sign of knowledge that a man who has no knowledge of a matter says: \"Allah knows best,\" for Allah said to His Prophet (ﷺ), (Say, I do not ask you for any reward for it, and I am not of the pretentious). Ibn Kathir: 4/45.\nThrough reflection on this verse, Abdullah bin Masoud deduced one of the etiquettes of pursuing knowledge. What is it?\nقُلۡ مَآ أَسۡـَٔلُكُمۡ عَلَيۡهِ مِنۡ أَجۡرٖ وَمَآ أَنَا۠ مِنَ ٱلۡمُتَكَلِّفِينَ ٨٦\n(And I am not of the pretentious), Islamic Sharia ordinances are free of affectation and hardship, which reflects the tolerance of Islam. This easiness is based on Allah's wisdom that the spirit of Sharia is in harmony with the nature of the Messenger (ﷺ). Ibn Ashur: 23/309.\nGiven this verse, describe the tolerance of Islam.\nإِنۡ هُوَ إِلَّا ذِكۡرٞ لِّلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ٨٧\nThis great Surah contains a wise reminder and a message of great importance. Therefore, at the beginning, it contains an oath that is full of reminders, and at the end, it describes it as a reminder to the worlds. The idea of reminding (and remembering) is mentioned frequently throughout, such as when Allah says: (Remember Our servant), (And remember Our servants), (as a mercy from Us and as a reminder) and (This is a reminder). Al-Saadi: 717.\nThis Surah enjoins something often. What is it? List two benefits from that.\nتَنزِيلُ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ مِنَ ٱللَّهِ ٱلۡعَزِيزِ ٱلۡحَكِيمِ ١\nSpeech is an attribute of the speaker, and the attribute is connected to the one who possesses that attribute. Therefore, just as Allah is perfect in all aspects, and there is none like unto Him, so too His word is perfect in all aspects, and there is nothing like it. This alone is sufficient to describe the Quran and highlight its sublime nature. Al-Saadi: 718.\nThis verse talks about the greatness of the Quran. Explain\nأَلَا لِلَّهِ ٱلدِّينُ ٱلۡخَالِصُۚ\nIbn Al-Arabi said: This verse proves that sincerity to Allah in every deed is obligatory. Al-Qurtubi: 18/246\nWhat heart’s deed is learned from this verse? Is it obligatory?\nإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَا يَهۡدِي مَنۡ هُوَ كَٰذِبٞ كَفَّارٞ ٣\nThere is no doubt that the more a servant fabricates lies about Allah and increases in disbelief in Him, the more Allah’s wrath upon him will increase, and hence, the divine guidance will be far away from him. Allah says, (How would Allah guide a people who disbelieved after having believed and testified that the Messenger was true, and the clear signs had come to them? For Allah does not guide the wrongdoing people) [3:86]. Ibn Ashur: 23/324.\nGiven this verse, explain the risk of fabricating lies about Allah.\nلَّوۡ أَرَادَ ٱللَّهُ أَن يَتَّخِذَ وَلَدٗا لَّٱصۡطَفَىٰ مِمَّا يَخۡلُقُ مَا يَشَآءُۚ سُبۡحَٰنَهُۥۖ هُوَ ٱللَّهُ ٱلۡوَٰحِدُ ٱلۡقَهَّارُ ٤\nAllah exalts Himself above the need to have a son; He describes Himself as the One, since Oneness contradicts having a son. If there were a son of Allah (glory to Him), he would have to be of the same type as Allah, but Allah does not belong to a type because He is One. He describes Himself as the Subjugator, in order to nullify all rivals and partners. If everything and everyone is subjugated by Allah, then, how can any of them be His partner? Ibn Juzay: 2/263.\nconcluding the verse with (the One, the Subjugator) has an insight into its meaning. Explain.\nwords\nأَجرٍA payment for guiding people to Allah\nالمُتَكَلِّفِينَA pretentious who falsely says something about Allah\nنَبَأَهُThe truth of the Quran\nمُخلِصًا لَهُ الدِّينَWorship Allah with sincere devotion to Him\nالدِّينُ الخَالِصُSincere devotion is due to Allah alone\nزُلفَىCloser to Allah\nلاَصطَفَىHe could have chosen\nيُكَوِّرُHe wraps"],[459,"§Az-Zumar\ndeeds\nBe kind to your mother in whose womb Allah created you.\nGive charity to a needy person in gratitude for Allah's successive favors upon you.\nPray during nighttime, and supplicate Allah, saying: \"O Allah, I hope for Your mercy and fear Your punishment, as Your definite punishment will strike the disbelievers.\"\nguid\nBe among those who know Allah during prosperity as they do during adversity.\nAllah elevates the status of people of knowledge, so, be one of them.\nBe among those who are patient, as they will be rewarded without measure.\nrefl\nوَأَنزَلَ لَكُم مِّنَ ٱلۡأَنۡعَٰمِ ثَمَٰنِيَةَ أَزۡوَٰجٖۚ\nThey are mentioned in Surat Al-An'am, (They are eight mates: a pair of sheep and a pair of goats), (and a pair of camels and a pair of cattle) [6:143,144]. Allah singled these out for mention, even though He also bestowed other animals upon His servants to serve their interests, because of their many benefits, for man finds many of his needs through them. Moreover, because of their honor, as they were singled out for certain purposes and no other animals can serve in their place - such as the Eid sacrifice, Hajj sacrifice, the sacrifice for the newborn, the fact that zakah applies to them, and because they may be given as blood money. Al-Saadi: 719.\nAmong all animals, Allah singles out these eight types for mention. Why?\nيَخۡلُقُكُمۡ فِي بُطُونِ أُمَّهَٰتِكُمۡ خَلۡقٗا مِّنۢ بَعۡدِ خَلۡقٖ فِي ظُلُمَٰتٖ ثَلَٰثٖۚ\n(Creation after creation), the creation of man begins from a sperm drop, then from a clinging clot, and then from a lump of flesh until his creation is complete, then Allah breathed into him of His spirit. Ibn Juzay: 2/264.\nThis verse shows the weakness of created beings and the power of the Creator. Explain.\nيَخۡلُقُكُمۡ فِي بُطُونِ أُمَّهَٰتِكُمۡ خَلۡقٗا مِّنۢ بَعۡدِ خَلۡقٖ فِي ظُلُمَٰتٖ ثَلَٰثٖۚ\n(In three layers of darkness), darkness of the belly, the womb and the membrane enclosing the fetus. Al-Jaza'iri : 4/468.\nThis verse mentions three layers of darkness. What are they?\nذَٰلِكُمُ ٱللَّهُ رَبُّكُمۡ لَهُ ٱلۡمُلۡكُۖ\nThe attribute of Lordship is mentioned as a reminder to them of the blessing of creation and provision, which is the meaning of Lordship. Moreover, it is a prelude for affirming their disbelief in the next verse, (If you disbelieve, then Allah is in no need of you, but He does not approve of disbelief for His servants). Ibn Ashur: 23/336.\nThis verse mentions Allah's attribute of Lordship. Why?\nأَمَّنۡ هُوَ قَٰنِتٌ ءَانَآءَ ٱلَّيۡلِ سَاجِدٗا وَقَآئِمٗا يَحۡذَرُ ٱلۡأٓخِرَةَ وَيَرۡجُواْ رَحۡمَةَ رَبِّهِۦۗ\nThe night is singled out for their prayer, because worship at nighttime stimulates the heart to remember Allah, is free of pretension, and indicates that worshiping Allah is preferred over comfort and going to sleep, as nighttime calls for rest, and when someone chooses worship instead, his heart becomes enlightened with the love to be closer to Allah. Allah says, (Indeed, worship at night is more effective and more conducive to proper recitation). Ibn Ashur: 23/346.\nThis verse singles out the night for the prayer. Why?\nلِلَّذِينَ أَحۡسَنُواْ فِي هَٰذِهِ ٱلدُّنۡيَا حَسَنَةٞۗ وَأَرۡضُ ٱللَّهِ وَٰسِعَةٌۗ\nThe text is general in meaning that anyone who does good will have good in this world - so what about those who believe in a land where they are persecuted and humiliated, and they do not get that good in this world? Therefore, this notion is warded off by the words, (Allah's earth is spacious). Allah states that His earth is spacious, so whenever you are prevented from worshiping Him in one place, then migrate to somewhere else.Al-Saadi: 721.\nAfter mentioning that whoever does good will have good, Allah mentions that His earth is spacious. Why?\nإِنَّمَا يُوَفَّى ٱلصَّٰبِرُونَ أَجۡرَهُم بِغَيۡرِ حِسَابٖ ١٠\nAli (t) said: \"Every obedient believer will be rewarded according to measure and scale, except those who are patient; their reward will be dispersed to them without account.\" It is narrated: \"The people who were afflicted will be brought, where no scale nor account will be set up for them, rather, their reward will be poured over them without account until the people who were safe in worldly life will wish that their bodies were cut with clippers in order to be rewarded the same as those who were afflicted.\" Al-Baghawi: 4/9.\nAllah will reward those who are patient without account. How?\nwords\nثَمَانِيَةَ أَزوَاجٍEight types of males and females; camels, cattle, sheep, and goats\nفِي ظُلُمَاتٍ ثَلاَثٍDarkness of the belly, the womb and the membrane enclosing the fetus\nفَأَنَّى تُصرَفُونَHow are you averted from worshiping Him\nخَوَّلَهُHe bestows upon him\nقَانِتٌDevoutly obedient\nيُوَفَّىWill be given"]])